window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":6,"qs":[{"id":"E4B-07","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"S3 Bucket Keys for SSE-KMS","q":"A data lake in Amazon S3 uses SSE-KMS with a customer managed key. Amazon Athena and Amazon EMR jobs read millions of small objects every day, and the AWS KMS request costs have grown significantly. The security team requires that the same customer managed key continues to be used for auditability. Which solution reduces costs MOST effectively?","o":["Change the bucket default encryption to SSE-S3.","Request a KMS request quota increase for the account.","Enable S3 Bucket Keys on the bucket for SSE-KMS and re-encrypt existing objects with a batch copy operation.","Switch the producers to client-side encryption with the AWS Encryption SDK."],"a":[2],"e":"Constraint penentu: kurangi biaya KMS tetapi 'the same customer managed key continues to be used'. S3 Bucket Keys membuat S3 menghasilkan bucket-level key berumur pendek dari KMS key Anda, sehingga S3 tidak perlu memanggil KMS untuk setiap objek; ini dapat menurunkan biaya request KMS hingga sekitar 99%. Kunci yang dipakai tetap customer managed key yang sama dan tetap tercatat di CloudTrail. Bucket Key berlaku untuk objek baru, jadi objek lama perlu disalin ulang (misalnya dengan S3 Batch Operations) agar ikut memakai Bucket Key. Distraktor terdekat adalah beralih ke SSE-S3: biaya KMS hilang tetapi melanggar syarat pemakaian customer managed key. Menaikkan quota hanya mengatasi throttling, bukan biaya. Client-side encryption menambah overhead dan tetap memanggil KMS untuk data key. Aturan umum: biaya/throttling KMS tinggi pada SSE-KMS → S3 Bucket Keys.","r":["Salah — SSE-S3 menghilangkan pemakaian customer managed key yang diwajibkan tim security.","Salah — Kenaikan quota mengatasi throttling, tetapi tidak menurunkan biaya per request KMS.","Benar — S3 Bucket Keys mengurangi panggilan KMS secara drastis sambil tetap memakai customer managed key yang sama.","Salah — Client-side encryption menambah kompleksitas, menyulitkan Athena/EMR, dan tidak menghilangkan panggilan KMS."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'SSE-KMS high KMS cost/throttling with many objects' → enable S3 Bucket Keys."},{"id":"E3B-67","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"Redshift distribution skew","q":"Queries against a large Amazon Redshift fact table are slow. The table uses DISTSTYLE KEY with order_status as the distribution key, and order_status has only five distinct values. A data engineer suspects that the data is unevenly distributed across node slices. Which TWO actions should the engineer take to confirm and fix the problem? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Query the SVV_TABLE_INFO system view and check the skew_rows column for the table.","Change the distribution to a high-cardinality column that is commonly used in joins, or to DISTSTYLE EVEN or AUTO, by using ALTER TABLE.","Run VACUUM SORT ONLY on the table.","Run ANALYZE on the table.","Add two more nodes to the cluster."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Gejalanya: DISTKEY pada kolom dengan kardinalitas rendah ('only five distinct values') sehingga data hanya tersebar ke beberapa slice dan sebagian slice menangani porsi besar. Untuk konfirmasi, SVV_TABLE_INFO menyediakan kolom skew_rows (rasio baris pada slice terbanyak dibanding slice tersedikit). Perbaikannya adalah ALTER TABLE untuk mengganti DISTKEY ke kolom berkardinalitas tinggi yang sering dipakai join, atau ke DISTSTYLE EVEN/AUTO bila tidak ada kunci join yang cocok. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah node: dengan hanya lima nilai kunci, data tetap hanya menempati paling banyak lima slice sehingga node tambahan tidak menyebarkan data. VACUUM dan ANALYZE tidak mengubah distribusi. Aturan: skew Redshift → cek skew_rows, pilih DISTKEY berkardinalitas tinggi atau EVEN/AUTO.","r":["Benar — skew_rows di SVV_TABLE_INFO mengonfirmasi ketidakseimbangan distribusi data antar slice.","Benar — Mengganti ke kolom berkardinalitas tinggi atau EVEN/AUTO menyebarkan data secara merata.","Salah — VACUUM SORT memperbaiki urutan sort, bukan distribusi antar slice.","Salah — ANALYZE memperbarui statistik, tidak memindahkan data antar slice.","Salah — Dengan lima nilai kunci, data tetap terkonsentrasi di sedikit slice meskipun node bertambah."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift skew → SVV_TABLE_INFO.skew_rows; jangan pakai DISTKEY berkardinalitas rendah."},{"id":"E1B-07","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"AWS Glue DataBrew","q":"A marketing team of business analysts with no programming experience needs to clean and normalize customer data stored in Amazon S3. They must remove duplicates, standardize date formats, and split full names into first and last names. They want to visually preview the effect of each step and reuse the steps on future datasets. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write an AWS Glue PySpark script that uses DynamicFrame transforms and schedule it as a job.","Use Amazon Athena CREATE TABLE AS SELECT statements with string functions.","Create an AWS Glue DataBrew project and save the transformation steps as a reusable recipe.","Use Amazon EMR Studio notebooks to explore and transform the data with Spark."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'no programming experience', 'visually preview the effect of each step', dan 'reuse the steps'. AWS Glue DataBrew adalah alat data preparation visual tanpa kode dengan ratusan transformasi bawaan, menampilkan preview hasil setiap langkah, dan menyimpan langkah-langkah sebagai recipe yang bisa dijalankan ulang sebagai job. Glue PySpark script adalah distraktor yang secara teknis bisa, tetapi membutuhkan kemampuan pemrograman. Athena CTAS membutuhkan SQL dan tidak memberi preview visual per langkah. EMR Studio notebook juga membutuhkan kode Spark. Aturan umum: analis non-programmer + pembersihan data visual → AWS Glue DataBrew.","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan kemampuan menulis PySpark, bertentangan dengan 'no programming experience'.","Salah — CTAS menuntut SQL dan tidak menyediakan preview visual per langkah transformasi.","Benar — DataBrew bersifat visual, no-code, menyediakan preview, dan recipe yang dapat dipakai ulang.","Salah — EMR Studio notebook adalah lingkungan berbasis kode untuk Spark."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'no-code, visual data preparation, recipe' → AWS Glue DataBrew."},{"id":"E3A-67","d":3,"ts":"3.2.6","t":"Grouping with ROLLUP and GROUPING SETS","q":"A finance report in Amazon Redshift must show total revenue for each region and product, a subtotal for each region, and a grand total, all produced by a single query. Which TWO GROUP BY clauses produce exactly these levels of aggregation? (Choose TWO.)","o":["GROUP BY ROLLUP (region, product)","GROUP BY region, product","GROUP BY GROUPING SETS ((region, product), (region), ())","GROUP BY CUBE (region, product)","GROUP BY region HAVING SUM(revenue) > 0"],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'region and product', 'subtotal for each region', 'grand total', 'single query', dan 'exactly these levels'. ROLLUP (region, product) menghasilkan agregasi hierarkis: (region, product), (region), dan () untuk grand total, persis tiga level yang diminta. GROUPING SETS ((region, product), (region), ()) menuliskan ketiga level yang sama secara eksplisit. CUBE (region, product) menghasilkan semua kombinasi, termasuk subtotal per product saja, sehingga ada level tambahan yang tidak diminta. GROUP BY region, product biasa hanya menghasilkan level detail tanpa subtotal atau grand total. HAVING hanya memfilter grup setelah agregasi dan tidak menambah level. Aturan umum: subtotal hierarkis → ROLLUP; semua kombinasi → CUBE; level kustom → GROUPING SETS.","r":["Benar — ROLLUP menghasilkan level (region, product), (region), dan grand total.","Salah — Hanya level detail, tanpa subtotal region atau grand total.","Benar — GROUPING SETS menyebutkan tepat ketiga level yang diminta.","Salah — CUBE menambahkan subtotal per product, level yang tidak diminta.","Salah — Hanya agregasi per region dengan filter, tanpa level detail atau grand total."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'subtotals + grand total in one query' → ROLLUP atau GROUPING SETS; CUBE = semua kombinasi."},{"id":"E3B-43","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"Glue Data Quality anomaly detection","q":"A daily AWS Glue job ingests partner transaction files. Normal daily row counts vary between 2 million and 9 million depending on the day of the week and promotions, so static thresholds keep producing false alarms. The team wants AWS Glue Data Quality to flag days when the row count is unusual compared to history. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Add the rule RowCount between 2000000 and 9000000 to the ruleset.","Add a RowCount analyzer and the rule DetectAnomalies \"RowCount\" to the Glue Data Quality ruleset in the job.","Enable CloudTrail Insights for AWS Glue.","Create a CloudWatch alarm with a static threshold on the job's bytes read metric."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'unusual compared to history' dan 'static thresholds keep producing false alarms'. Glue Data Quality anomaly detection menggunakan analyzer (misalnya RowCount) untuk mengumpulkan statistik setiap run dan rule DetectAnomalies \"RowCount\" untuk menandai nilai yang menyimpang dari pola historis; diperlukan beberapa titik data historis sebelum deteksi efektif. Distraktor terdekat adalah RowCount between dengan rentang tetap — justru pendekatan statis yang menimbulkan masalah dan tidak menangkap penurunan tidak wajar yang masih dalam rentang. CloudTrail Insights menganalisis panggilan API, bukan isi data. Alarm statis bytes read memiliki masalah yang sama. Aturan: kualitas data dengan pola dinamis → Glue DQ anomaly detection (Analyzers + DetectAnomalies).","r":["Salah — Rentang statis tidak menyesuaikan pola harian dan bisa melewatkan anomali di dalam rentang.","Benar — Analyzer RowCount dengan DetectAnomalies mempelajari histori dan menandai jumlah baris yang tidak wajar.","Salah — CloudTrail Insights tidak menganalisis statistik data.","Salah — Threshold statis tetap memicu false alarm pada pola yang bervariasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'unusual compared to history' di Glue DQ → Analyzers + DetectAnomalies."},{"id":"E1B-42","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Converting to Apache Iceberg","q":"A company stores customer order data as daily CSV files in Amazon S3. New requirements state that the data lake must support row-level updates and deletes for GDPR requests, ACID transactions for concurrent writers, and time travel queries from Amazon Athena. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Keep the CSV format and overwrite the entire dataset each time a record must be deleted.","Convert the data to Parquet partitioned by date and rewrite affected partitions with a custom script.","Use an AWS Glue ETL job to convert the data into Apache Iceberg tables registered in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, and use MERGE and DELETE statements.","Convert the data to JSON Lines files and use S3 Object Lock to manage versions."],"a":[2],"e":"Persyaratan penentunya adalah 'row-level updates and deletes', 'ACID transactions for concurrent writers', dan 'time travel queries from Amazon Athena'. Apache Iceberg adalah open table format yang menambahkan lapisan metadata di atas file Parquet sehingga mendukung transaksi ACID, operasi MERGE/UPDATE/DELETE tingkat baris, evolusi skema, serta time travel, dan Athena maupun Glue mendukungnya secara native. Parquet terpartisi dengan skrip kustom adalah distraktor terdekat karena efisien untuk query, tetapi tidak memberi ACID atau time travel dan menulis ulang partisi secara manual rawan konflik. Menulis ulang seluruh CSV sangat mahal dan tidak transaksional. Object Lock mencegah penghapusan, yang justru bertentangan dengan kebutuhan GDPR. Aturan umum: ACID, upsert/delete, time travel di data lake → Iceberg (termasuk S3 Tables).","r":["Salah — Menulis ulang seluruh dataset mahal, lambat, dan tidak memberi ACID atau time travel.","Salah — Parquet biasa tidak mendukung transaksi ACID maupun time travel; skrip kustom rawan konflik.","Benar — Iceberg mendukung ACID, MERGE/DELETE tingkat baris, dan time travel yang dapat di-query Athena.","Salah — JSON Lines tidak transaksional, dan Object Lock mencegah penghapusan yang diwajibkan GDPR."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ACID + row-level delete/upsert + time travel on S3' → Apache Iceberg."},{"id":"E2C-41","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Vectorization pipeline in Bedrock knowledge bases","q":"A company wants employees to ask natural-language questions about 50,000 internal policy documents stored in Amazon S3. The data engineer sets up an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. During ingestion, which sequence correctly describes how the documents are prepared so that semantically similar content can be retrieved?","o":["The documents are compressed with gzip, indexed by file name in Amazon DynamoDB, and retrieved with exact keyword matching.","The documents are split into chunks, each chunk is converted into a numeric vector by an embeddings model, and the vectors are written to a vector store with a mapping back to the source document.","The documents are converted to Parquet, cataloged by an AWS Glue crawler, and queried with Amazon Athena SQL.","A text-generation model summarizes each document into one sentence, and the summaries are stored in an Amazon RDS table."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'semantically similar content can be retrieved', yang merupakan inti konsep vectorization. Saat ingestion, Amazon Bedrock knowledge base memecah dokumen menjadi chunk, lalu embeddings model (misalnya Amazon Titan Text Embeddings V2) mengubah setiap chunk menjadi vektor numerik yang merepresentasikan makna teks. Vektor disimpan di vector store bersama mapping ke dokumen sumber, sehingga saat query, pertanyaan pengguna juga di-embed dan dicari vektor terdekat (similarity search). Keyword matching pada nama file tidak menangkap makna semantik. Athena SQL bekerja pada data terstruktur, bukan pencarian kemiripan makna. Ringkasan satu kalimat di RDS kehilangan detail dan tetap tidak mendukung similarity search. Aturan umum: vectorization = chunking → embedding → simpan di vector index → similarity search.","r":["Salah — Kompresi dan keyword matching tidak menghasilkan representasi semantik.","Benar — Chunking, embedding, dan penyimpanan vektor dengan mapping ke sumber adalah alur ingestion knowledge base.","Salah — Athena SQL tidak melakukan pencarian berdasarkan kemiripan makna.","Salah — Ringkasan satu kalimat kehilangan detail dan tidak mendukung similarity search."],"k":"Tips ujian: knowledge base ingestion → chunk → embeddings model → vector store."},{"id":"E3A-19","d":3,"ts":"3.1.5","t":"Consuming SaaS APIs with AppFlow","q":"A marketing team needs daily copies of opportunity and account records from Salesforce in an Amazon S3 data lake, stored as Parquet. Only records changed since the last run should be transferred. The team has no developers available to maintain custom API clients, OAuth token refresh logic, or pagination code. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an Amazon AppFlow flow with the Salesforce connector, a scheduled trigger with incremental transfer, and Amazon S3 as the destination in Parquet format.","Write an AWS Lambda function that calls the Salesforce REST API, handles OAuth refresh and pagination, and writes Parquet files to S3.","Use AWS DMS with Salesforce as the source endpoint and S3 as the target.","Run an AWS Glue crawler against the Salesforce API endpoint and query the result with Athena."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'Salesforce' (SaaS), 'only changed records', 'Parquet', dan 'no developers to maintain API clients'. Amazon AppFlow adalah layanan terkelola untuk memindahkan data dari aplikasi SaaS seperti Salesforce ke AWS tanpa kode. AppFlow menangani autentikasi OAuth, pagination, dan mendukung schedule trigger dengan incremental transfer serta tujuan S3 dalam format Parquet. Lambda bisa melakukannya, tetapi tim harus membuat dan merawat kode OAuth, pagination, dan retry, yang justru ingin dihindari. AWS DMS untuk migrasi database, tidak mendukung Salesforce sebagai source. Glue crawler membaca metadata dari data store, bukan menarik data dari REST API SaaS. Aturan umum: data dari SaaS (Salesforce, ServiceNow, Zendesk, dan sebagainya) ke S3/Redshift tanpa kode → Amazon AppFlow.","r":["Benar — AppFlow menangani koneksi Salesforce, transfer incremental terjadwal, dan output Parquet ke S3 tanpa kode.","Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi tim harus merawat kode OAuth, pagination, dan error handling.","Salah — DMS ditujukan untuk database, bukan aplikasi SaaS seperti Salesforce.","Salah — Crawler tidak bisa menarik data dari API SaaS; ia hanya mengisi metadata Data Catalog."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'SaaS (Salesforce) → S3, no code, incremental' → Amazon AppFlow."},{"id":"E4A-59","d":4,"ts":"4.2.6","t":"Least-privilege S3 prefix policies","q":"Team A's IAM role must be able to list and read only the objects under the team-a/ prefix of the shared bucket datalake-shared, including in the S3 console. It must not see the names of objects under other teams' prefixes. Which TWO policy statements meet these requirements while following least privilege? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Allow s3:ListBucket on arn:aws:s3:::datalake-shared with a condition that s3:prefix matches team-a/*.","Allow s3:ListBucket on arn:aws:s3:::datalake-shared/team-a/*.","Allow s3:GetObject on arn:aws:s3:::datalake-shared.","Allow s3:* on arn:aws:s3:::datalake-shared/team-a/*.","Allow s3:GetObject on arn:aws:s3:::datalake-shared/team-a/*."],"a":[0,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'list and read only' di prefix team-a/ dan 'must not see the names' di prefix lain. s3:ListBucket adalah aksi level bucket, sehingga resource-nya harus ARN bucket; pembatasan per prefix dilakukan dengan kondisi s3:prefix. s3:GetObject adalah aksi level objek, sehingga resource-nya ARN objek dengan path team-a/*. ListBucket pada ARN objek tidak pernah cocok sehingga listing gagal. GetObject pada ARN bucket tidak cocok dengan objek apa pun. s3:* pada prefix memberi izin menulis dan menghapus yang tidak dibutuhkan. Aturan umum: ListBucket → ARN bucket + kondisi s3:prefix; GetObject/PutObject → ARN objek (bucket/prefix/*).","r":["Benar — ListBucket pada ARN bucket dengan kondisi s3:prefix membatasi listing hanya pada team-a/.","Salah — ListBucket adalah aksi level bucket dan tidak cocok dengan ARN objek.","Salah — GetObject adalah aksi level objek dan tidak cocok dengan ARN bucket.","Salah — s3:* memberi izin tulis dan hapus yang melanggar least privilege.","Benar — GetObject pada ARN objek team-a/* memberi akses baca tepat sesuai kebutuhan."],"k":"Tips ujian: ListBucket = ARN bucket + s3:prefix; GetObject = ARN objek; jangan tukar resource-nya."},{"id":"E2A-18","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"Aurora endpoints","q":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster with one writer and four Aurora Replicas. Two of the replicas use a larger instance class and are intended only for long-running reporting queries. The other two replicas serve short, latency-sensitive application reads. Currently, all read traffic uses the cluster reader endpoint and reports slow down application reads. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Point the reporting tool at the cluster writer endpoint.","Create an Aurora custom endpoint that includes only the two larger replicas and point the reporting tool at it.","Enable Aurora Auto Scaling for replicas so the reader endpoint adds more instances.","Convert the two larger replicas into an Aurora global database secondary cluster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah dua replica khusus untuk 'long-running reporting queries' dan masalahnya adalah reader endpoint menyeimbangkan koneksi ke semua replica. Aurora custom endpoint memungkinkan pengelompokan sekumpulan instance tertentu di bawah satu endpoint, sehingga traffic laporan hanya diarahkan ke dua replica besar, sementara aplikasi tetap memakai replica lain. Distraktor terdekat adalah Auto Scaling replica: menambah instance, tetapi reader endpoint tetap mencampur laporan dan query aplikasi pada instance yang sama. Writer endpoint justru membebani instance penulis. Global database ditujukan untuk replikasi lintas Region dan disaster recovery, bukan isolasi workload dalam satu Region. Aturan umum: isolasi workload baca tertentu ke subset replica Aurora → custom endpoint.","r":["Salah — Menjalankan laporan berat di writer mengganggu transaksi tulis aplikasi.","Benar — Custom endpoint mengarahkan koneksi laporan hanya ke replica besar sehingga workload terisolasi.","Salah — Auto Scaling menambah replica, tetapi reader endpoint tetap menyebarkan laporan ke semua replica termasuk yang melayani aplikasi.","Salah — Global database untuk replikasi lintas Region; berlebihan dan tidak memecahkan routing di dalam cluster."],"k":"Route specific workload to a subset of Aurora replicas → Aurora custom endpoint."},{"id":"E3B-29","d":3,"ts":"3.3.4","t":"Glue job performance - splittable input","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job that processes a single 40 GB gzip-compressed CSV file takes 3 hours. Glue job metrics show that one executor is busy while all other executors are idle for almost the entire run. Adding more workers did not reduce the runtime. What should a data engineer do to improve performance?","o":["Change the worker type from G.1X to G.2X.","Enable job bookmarks for the job.","Increase the job timeout to 6 hours.","Have the producer deliver the data as many smaller files or in a splittable format, such as bzip2-compressed CSV or Parquet, so that Spark can parallelize the read."],"a":[3],"e":"Gejala kuncinya: 'one executor is busy while all other executors are idle' dan 'adding more workers did not reduce the runtime'. File gzip tidak dapat dipecah (non-splittable), sehingga Spark membaca seluruh file 40 GB dengan satu task di satu executor. Solusinya adalah membuat input bisa diparalelkan: banyak file kecil, kompresi splittable (bzip2), atau format kolumnar seperti Parquet. Distraktor terdekat adalah worker G.2X: memberi lebih banyak memori dan vCPU per worker, tetapi tetap hanya satu task yang membaca file sehingga hampir tidak membantu. Bookmarks dan timeout tidak menyentuh akar masalah. Aturan: satu executor sibuk + gzip besar → masalah splittability.","r":["Salah — Worker lebih besar tidak memecah file gzip, jadi pembacaan tetap dilakukan oleh satu task.","Salah — Bookmarks hanya melacak data yang sudah diproses.","Salah — Menambah timeout hanya mencegah kegagalan, bukan mempercepat job.","Benar — Input splittable atau banyak file memungkinkan Spark membagi pembacaan ke banyak executor."],"k":"Tips ujian: gzip = non-splittable → satu task; gunakan banyak file, bzip2, atau Parquet."},{"id":"E3A-07","d":3,"ts":"3.1.2","t":"MWAA worker autoscaling","q":"An Amazon MWAA environment runs many DAGs that start at 01:00 every night. During that hour, many tasks stay in the queued state for a long time, while CPU utilization on the scheduler is low. During the rest of the day, the environment is mostly idle. The company wants to reduce queue time without paying for extra capacity all day. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Increase the minimum worker count so that it equals the expected peak number of workers.","Reduce the number of DAGs that run at 01:00 by converting half of them to AWS Glue workflows.","Increase the maximum worker count of the environment so that MWAA worker autoscaling can add workers during the peak.","Increase the schedule interval of the DAGs so that they run every two days."],"a":[2],"e":"Gejala 'tasks stay queued' saat 'scheduler CPU is low' menunjukkan kekurangan kapasitas worker untuk mengeksekusi task, bukan masalah scheduler. MWAA punya autoscaling worker antara minimum dan maximum worker count. Menaikkan maximum workers membuat MWAA menambah worker saat antrean tinggi pada jam 01:00 dan menurunkannya lagi saat idle, sehingga sesuai syarat 'without paying for extra capacity all day'. Menaikkan minimum workers ke nilai puncak memang mengurangi antrean, tetapi worker ekstra dibayar sepanjang hari. Memindahkan DAG ke Glue atau mengubah jadwal mengubah kebutuhan bisnis. Aturan umum: task MWAA lama di status queued → naikkan max workers (autoscaling) atau environment class; minimum workers hanya untuk baseline.","r":["Salah — Minimum worker tinggi membuat kapasitas puncak dibayar sepanjang hari.","Salah — Migrasi ke Glue workflows adalah perubahan besar yang tidak diperlukan.","Benar — Max worker count yang lebih tinggi memungkinkan autoscaling saat puncak lalu turun lagi saat idle.","Salah — Mengubah jadwal mengorbankan kebutuhan bisnis dan tidak menyelesaikan kekurangan worker."],"k":"Tips ujian: MWAA 'tasks queued' + scheduler santai → naikkan maximum workers; jangan naikkan minimum jika beban hanya sesaat."},{"id":"E3A-41","d":3,"ts":"3.2.1","t":"Quick Sight ML insights forecasting","q":"A finance team uses an Amazon Quick Sight analysis that shows monthly revenue for the last 4 years. The team wants to display the expected revenue for the next 6 months with confidence bands directly on the line chart. The team has no data science skills and wants to avoid building ML pipelines. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Add an ML-powered forecast to the line chart visual in Quick Sight and set the forecast length to 6 periods.","Train a forecasting model in Amazon SageMaker AI and write predictions to S3 for Quick Sight to read.","Use Amazon Forecast to create a predictor and import the results into Quick Sight.","Add a calculated field that multiplies last year's revenue by a fixed growth rate."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'expected revenue for the next 6 months', 'confidence bands on the line chart', 'no data science skills', dan 'avoid building ML pipelines'. Quick Sight memiliki ML insights bawaan, termasuk forecasting yang bisa ditambahkan langsung ke visual line chart time series dengan pengaturan panjang periode dan prediction interval. Tidak perlu model atau pipeline terpisah. SageMaker AI membutuhkan keahlian ML dan pipeline. Amazon Forecast sudah tidak menerima pelanggan baru sejak 2024, jadi bukan pilihan untuk solusi baru dan juga menambah pipeline. Pengalian growth rate tetap adalah estimasi kasar tanpa confidence band. Aturan umum: forecast atau anomaly detection sederhana di dashboard → ML insights bawaan Quick Sight.","r":["Benar — Forecast ML bawaan Quick Sight menambahkan prediksi dan confidence band langsung di line chart tanpa pipeline.","Salah — Membutuhkan keahlian dan pipeline ML yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Amazon Forecast tidak menerima pelanggan baru dan menambah pipeline terpisah.","Salah — Growth rate tetap tidak menghasilkan forecast statistik maupun confidence band."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'forecast / anomaly on dashboard, no ML skills' → Quick Sight ML insights."},{"id":"E2A-07","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Aurora vs RDS vs DynamoDB","q":"A company's order management application uses MySQL and relies on ACID transactions, foreign keys, and multi-table joins. The company needs high availability across Availability Zones, the ability to add up to 15 low-latency read replicas, and storage that grows automatically without downtime. Which data store should a data engineer recommend?","o":["Amazon Aurora MySQL-Compatible Edition","Amazon DynamoDB with transactions enabled","Amazon RDS for MySQL in a Single-AZ deployment","Amazon Redshift with a Multi-AZ deployment"],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'MySQL', 'ACID transactions, foreign keys, and multi-table joins', 'up to 15 low-latency read replicas', dan storage yang 'grows automatically'. Amazon Aurora MySQL kompatibel dengan MySQL, menyimpan data enam salinan di tiga AZ, mendukung hingga 15 Aurora Replicas yang berbagi cluster volume yang sama (replica lag rendah), dan storage tumbuh otomatis. Distraktor terdekat adalah RDS for MySQL Single-AZ: kompatibel, tetapi tidak memberikan ketersediaan lintas AZ; RDS for MySQL memang juga mendukung hingga 15 read replica, namun replikasinya asinkron berbasis binlog sehingga lag-nya umumnya lebih tinggi dibanding Aurora Replicas yang berbagi cluster volume. DynamoDB mendukung transaksi tetapi tidak mendukung foreign key atau join SQL. Redshift adalah data warehouse OLAP, bukan database transaksional. Aturan umum: OLTP relasional kompatibel MySQL/PostgreSQL dengan HA dan banyak replica → Aurora.","r":["Benar — Aurora MySQL memberikan kompatibilitas MySQL, HA lintas AZ, hingga 15 read replica latensi rendah, dan storage auto-growing.","Salah — DynamoDB tidak mendukung join dan foreign key sehingga aplikasi relasional harus didesain ulang.","Salah — Single-AZ tidak memenuhi kebutuhan high availability lintas AZ.","Salah — Redshift adalah data warehouse analitik dan tidak cocok untuk transaksi OLTP aplikasi order."],"k":"Relational OLTP + HA + up to 15 replicas + auto-growing storage → Amazon Aurora."},{"id":"E1A-43","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Lambda Kinesis error handling","q":"A Lambda function processes batches from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. A single malformed record causes the function to throw an error, and the entire shard stops making progress while Lambda retries the same batch until the record expires. The team wants to isolate bad records, keep processing the rest of the shard, and keep a copy of the failed records for later analysis. Which TWO configuration changes should the data engineer make on the event source mapping? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Increase the stream retention period to 365 days.","Increase the Lambda function memory to 10 GB.","Enable BisectBatchOnFunctionError so that failing batches are split to isolate the bad record.","Change the stream to on-demand capacity mode.","Set MaximumRetryAttempts (and optionally MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds) and configure an on-failure destination such as an Amazon SQS queue."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Kata kunci: satu 'malformed record' membuat 'entire shard stops making progress', ingin 'isolate bad records', 'keep processing', dan 'keep a copy'. Secara default, Lambda me-retry batch yang gagal hingga record kedaluwarsa, sehingga shard macet (poison pill). BisectBatchOnFunctionError membagi batch yang gagal menjadi dua secara berulang sehingga record bermasalah terisolasi. MaximumRetryAttempts atau MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds membatasi retry, dan on-failure destination (misalnya SQS atau SNS) menyimpan metadata batch yang gagal untuk analisis, lalu shard lanjut diproses. Distraktor terdekat adalah memperpanjang retensi: hanya memperpanjang waktu macet. Menambah memory atau mengubah capacity mode tidak memperbaiki record rusak. Aturan umum: poison record di Kinesis/DynamoDB Streams = bisect + batasi retry + on-failure destination.","r":["Salah — Retensi lebih lama membuat retry pada record rusak berlangsung lebih lama, bukan menyelesaikan masalah.","Salah — Memory tambahan tidak memperbaiki error karena data yang malformed.","Benar — Bisect batch mengisolasi record rusak sehingga record lain di batch tetap bisa diproses.","Salah — Capacity mode tidak memengaruhi penanganan error di Lambda.","Benar — Membatasi retry dan mengirim info batch gagal ke on-failure destination membuat shard tetap berjalan dan kegagalan tercatat."],"k":"Poison record pada Kinesis + Lambda → BisectBatchOnFunctionError + MaximumRetryAttempts + on-failure destination."},{"id":"E1B-18","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Athena JDBC/ODBC connectivity","q":"A finance team uses a third-party desktop BI tool on Windows that supports only ODBC connections. The team needs to run interactive SQL queries on data that is stored in Amazon S3 and cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. The company does not want to load the data into another database. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Connect the BI tool directly to the S3 bucket by using the bucket's HTTPS endpoint.","Install and configure the Amazon Athena ODBC driver on the analysts' computers and connect the BI tool to Athena.","Install the Amazon Redshift ODBC driver and connect it to the S3 bucket.","Schedule a daily AWS Glue job that exports query results as CSV files to a shared network drive."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci yang menentukan adalah 'supports only ODBC', 'interactive SQL queries', data di S3 yang sudah ter-katalog di Glue Data Catalog, dan tidak ingin memuat data ke database lain. Amazon Athena menyediakan driver ODBC (dan JDBC) resmi sehingga tool BI dapat menjalankan SQL langsung terhadap tabel Glue Data Catalog yang datanya ada di S3. Driver ODBC Redshift adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi driver itu terhubung ke cluster/workgroup Redshift, bukan langsung ke S3, dan memakai Spectrum berarti menambah Redshift. S3 bukan engine SQL sehingga tidak bisa dihubungkan langsung oleh tool BI. Ekspor CSV harian tidak interaktif dan datanya tidak segar. Aturan umum: tool pihak ketiga ke Athena → Athena JDBC/ODBC driver.","r":["Salah — S3 adalah object storage, bukan endpoint SQL; tool BI tidak dapat menjalankan query SQL langsung ke bucket.","Benar — Driver ODBC Athena memungkinkan query SQL interaktif atas data S3 yang terdaftar di Glue Data Catalog.","Salah — Driver Redshift terhubung ke Redshift, bukan langsung ke S3, dan berarti menambah layanan database.","Salah — Ekspor harian tidak interaktif dan menghasilkan data yang basi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'BI tool via JDBC/ODBC + data in S3' → Athena JDBC/ODBC driver."},{"id":"E1A-17","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"AWS DMS full load tuning","q":"A data engineer uses AWS DMS to perform a full load of a 5 TB on-premises PostgreSQL database to Amazon S3. Many large tables are loaded one after another, and the full load phase takes too long. The replication instance has spare CPU and memory, and network bandwidth is not saturated. Which change will MOST improve full load performance?","o":["Change the task type from full load to CDC only.","Increase the MaxFullLoadSubTasks task setting and configure parallel load for the largest tables by using table-level segmentation.","Enable the ValidationEnabled task setting.","Change the target format from Parquet to CSV."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: tabel besar dimuat 'one after another', sementara 'spare CPU and memory' dan bandwidth belum penuh. MaxFullLoadSubTasks mengatur berapa banyak tabel yang dimuat secara paralel, sedangkan parallel load membagi satu tabel besar menjadi beberapa segmen (berdasarkan partisi atau rentang kolom) yang dimuat bersamaan. Keduanya memanfaatkan kapasitas idle replication instance. Distraktor terdekat yaitu validasi justru menambah beban karena membandingkan data sumber dan target. CDC only tidak memuat data yang sudah ada sehingga tidak memenuhi kebutuhan full load. Mengganti format target tidak menyelesaikan bottleneck pemuatan serial. Aturan umum: full load DMS lambat dengan resource tersisa = naikkan paralelisme (MaxFullLoadSubTasks, parallel load).","r":["Salah — CDC only tidak memuat data yang sudah ada, sehingga full load tidak terjadi.","Benar — Menambah sub-task paralel dan parallel load per segmen memanfaatkan kapasitas yang masih menganggur.","Salah — Validasi menambah beban kerja dan memperlambat task.","Salah — Format target bukan penyebab pemuatan serial tabel."],"k":"DMS full load lambat, resource masih ada → MaxFullLoadSubTasks + parallel load."},{"id":"E1A-53","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"DynamoDB throttling and backoff","q":"A data engineer runs a nightly batch job that loads 20 million items into an Amazon DynamoDB table with provisioned capacity by using BatchWriteItem. Some calls return UnprocessedItems, and the job logs ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors. The job must load every item without increasing the table's provisioned capacity. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Ignore UnprocessedItems because DynamoDB retries them automatically in the background.","Retry the UnprocessedItems with exponential backoff and jitter until all items are written.","Switch from BatchWriteItem to Scan operations.","Send all requests in parallel from as many threads as possible to finish faster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'UnprocessedItems' dan 'ProvisionedThroughputExceededException', dengan syarat 'load every item without increasing the table's provisioned capacity'. Saat kapasitas tulis terlampaui, BatchWriteItem mengembalikan item yang belum ditulis dalam UnprocessedItems; aplikasi wajib mengirim ulang item tersebut. Exponential backoff dengan jitter memberi waktu kapasitas pulih dan menghindari retry serentak yang memperparah throttling (AWS SDK sudah memiliki retry bawaan untuk exception, tetapi UnprocessedItems harus ditangani aplikasi). Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah paralelisme sebanyak mungkin: justru memperparah throttling. DynamoDB tidak me-retry UnprocessedItems secara otomatis, sehingga mengabaikannya menyebabkan data hilang. Scan adalah operasi baca. Aturan umum: throttling DynamoDB tanpa menambah kapasitas = retry dengan exponential backoff + jitter (dan sebarkan beban).","r":["Salah — DynamoDB tidak menulis ulang UnprocessedItems secara otomatis; mengabaikannya menyebabkan data hilang.","Benar — Retry UnprocessedItems dengan exponential backoff dan jitter menyelesaikan pemuatan tanpa menambah kapasitas.","Salah — Scan adalah operasi baca, tidak menulis data.","Salah — Paralelisme berlebih memperparah throttling pada kapasitas yang sama."],"k":"DynamoDB UnprocessedItems / throttling → retry dengan exponential backoff + jitter."},{"id":"E1B-53","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Spark join optimization","q":"A Spark job on AWS Glue joins a 2 TB fact table with a 40 MB product dimension table. The job spends most of its time in a shuffle stage, and executors spill large amounts of data to disk. Which change will MOST improve the job's performance?","o":["Use a broadcast join so that the small dimension table is sent to every executor and the large fact table is not shuffled.","Repartition both tables into a single partition before the join.","Convert both tables to CSV before the join.","Disable Spark adaptive query execution."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah join antara tabel besar '2 TB' dan tabel kecil '40 MB' dengan waktu yang habis pada 'shuffle stage' dan spill ke disk. Broadcast join mengirim salinan tabel kecil ke setiap executor sehingga tabel besar tidak perlu di-shuffle melalui jaringan; join dilakukan secara lokal pada setiap partisi tabel fakta. Repartition ke satu partisi justru menghilangkan paralelisme dan membuat satu task memproses semua data. CSV lebih besar dan lebih lambat dibaca daripada format kolumnar. Menonaktifkan adaptive query execution menghilangkan optimasi otomatis Spark, termasuk konversi ke broadcast join. Aturan umum: join tabel besar dengan tabel kecil → broadcast join untuk menghindari shuffle.","r":["Benar — Broadcast join menghindari shuffle tabel besar dan mengurangi spill.","Salah — Satu partisi menghilangkan paralelisme dan memperburuk kinerja.","Salah — CSV memperbesar I/O dan tidak mengurangi shuffle.","Salah — AQE membantu mengoptimalkan join; menonaktifkannya memperburuk kinerja."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'large table JOIN small table + heavy shuffle' → broadcast join."},{"id":"E2A-28","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Purpose-built database selection","q":"A data engineer is reviewing proposed data store choices for several new workloads. Which TWO proposals correctly match the workload to an appropriate AWS data store? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use Amazon Keyspaces to run ad-hoc SQL queries that join many relational tables.","Use Amazon Neptune to power 'customers who know your friends also bought' recommendations based on a social graph.","Use Amazon DocumentDB as a petabyte-scale columnar data warehouse for BI dashboards.","Use Amazon DynamoDB as a serverless session store that is read and written by session ID at any scale, with Time to Live (TTL) to remove inactive sessions automatically.","Use Amazon Redshift to serve 100,000 single-row lookups per second for a mobile application."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Soal ini menguji pemetaan karakteristik workload ke purpose-built database. Rekomendasi berbasis relasi sosial ('customers who know your friends') adalah pola traversal graph, sehingga Amazon Neptune tepat. Session store yang diakses 'by session ID' dengan skala besar adalah pola key-value klasik untuk Amazon DynamoDB, dan TTL otomatis menghapus item sesi yang kedaluwarsa tanpa mengonsumsi write capacity. Distraktor terdekat adalah Redshift untuk lookup baris tunggal: Redshift adalah warehouse kolumnar yang dioptimalkan untuk scan dan agregasi besar, bukan ratusan ribu point lookup per detik dari aplikasi. Keyspaces (Cassandra) tidak mendukung join relasional, dan DocumentDB bukan data warehouse kolumnar. Aturan umum: pilih database berdasarkan pola akses — graph → Neptune, key-value serverless → DynamoDB, OLAP → Redshift, document → DocumentDB, wide-column → Keyspaces.","r":["Salah — Keyspaces adalah wide-column store kompatibel Cassandra yang tidak mendukung join antar tabel.","Benar — Rekomendasi berbasis social graph adalah use case klasik graph database seperti Neptune.","Salah — DocumentDB adalah document database untuk data JSON operasional, bukan warehouse kolumnar untuk BI.","Benar — Akses key-value berdasarkan session ID dengan skala tak terduga cocok untuk DynamoDB, dan TTL menghapus sesi kedaluwarsa tanpa biaya write.","Salah — Redshift tidak dirancang untuk point lookup berkonkurensi sangat tinggi dari aplikasi; DynamoDB lebih tepat."],"k":"Match access pattern: graph → Neptune; key-value session store + expiry → DynamoDB + TTL; OLAP → Redshift."},{"id":"E2B-41","d":2,"ts":"2.3.3","t":"Lifecycle expiration with versioning","q":"A data engineer added an S3 Lifecycle rule that expires current object versions after 30 days in a bucket with S3 Versioning enabled. Two months later, the bucket's storage bill has not decreased, and S3 Storage Lens shows that noncurrent versions are growing. Which change will reduce storage MOST effectively while still allowing recovery of deleted objects for 7 days?","o":["Suspend versioning on the bucket so that the existing noncurrent versions are deleted.","Change the expiration rule to 1 day so that objects are removed sooner.","Add a NoncurrentVersionExpiration action of 7 days and configure the Lifecycle configuration to remove expired object delete markers.","Transition current versions to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 30 days instead of expiring them."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'Versioning enabled', 'noncurrent versions are growing' dan 'allowing recovery ... for 7 days'. Pada bucket berversi, Expiration atas versi current tidak menghapus data; S3 hanya menambahkan delete marker, dan versi lama menjadi noncurrent yang tetap ditagih. Untuk benar-benar menghapus, tambahkan NoncurrentVersionExpiration (misalnya 7 hari setelah menjadi noncurrent), sehingga ada jendela pemulihan 7 hari, lalu hapus expired object delete markers agar marker yatim tidak menumpuk. Suspend versioning tidak menghapus versi yang sudah ada. Expiration 1 hari hanya membuat delete marker lebih cepat. Transisi current version tidak menyentuh versi noncurrent. Ingat: versioned bucket → Expiration = delete marker; hapus data lama dengan NoncurrentVersionExpiration.","r":["Salah — Suspend versioning tidak menghapus versi noncurrent yang sudah ada.","Salah — Expiration lebih cepat hanya menambah delete marker; versi lama tetap tersimpan.","Benar — NoncurrentVersionExpiration 7 hari menghapus versi lama setelah jendela pemulihan, dan delete marker kedaluwarsa ikut dibersihkan.","Salah — Transisi versi current tidak mengatasi versi noncurrent yang terus bertambah."],"k":"Tips ujian: versioned bucket biaya tidak turun setelah expiration → tambahkan NoncurrentVersionExpiration + hapus expired delete markers."},{"id":"E1B-63","d":1,"ts":"1.2.9","t":"Handling data variety","q":"A company ingests product feeds from more than 200 suppliers. Each supplier sends JSON files with a different structure, and suppliers frequently add, rename, or nest fields without notice. A fixed relational schema has caused frequent load failures. The company wants a scalable way to store and process this variety of data with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Land the raw files in an Amazon S3 data lake, use AWS Glue crawlers to infer and track schemas, and process the data with AWS Glue DynamicFrames that tolerate schema differences.","Create a separate Amazon RDS table for each supplier and update the table definitions manually when schemas change.","Reject any file that does not match a single master schema and ask the supplier to resend it.","Convert all files to CSV with a fixed set of columns before storing them in Amazon Redshift."],"a":[0],"e":"Penentunya adalah 'more than 200 suppliers' dengan struktur berbeda (variety tinggi) yang sering berubah tanpa pemberitahuan, kegagalan load karena 'fixed relational schema', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Data lake di S3 menyimpan data mentah apa adanya (schema-on-read), Glue crawler menginferensi dan melacak perubahan skema di Data Catalog, dan DynamicFrame dapat menangani field yang berbeda atau berubah tanpa skema tetap di awal. Tabel RDS per supplier dengan pembaruan manual menciptakan beban operasional yang besar. Menolak file mengganggu bisnis dan tidak skalabel. Memaksa CSV dengan kolom tetap membuang field baru dan struktur bersarang. Aturan umum: variety tinggi dan skema berubah-ubah → data lake S3 + schema-on-read (Glue crawler/Data Catalog, DynamicFrame).","r":["Benar — S3 data lake dengan schema-on-read, crawler, dan DynamicFrame menangani variasi skema dengan overhead rendah.","Salah — 200 tabel dengan pembaruan manual menimbulkan beban operasional tinggi.","Salah — Menolak file mengganggu operasional dan tidak menyelesaikan masalah variety.","Salah — Kolom tetap membuang field baru dan struktur bersarang."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'many sources, different/changing schemas (variety)' → S3 data lake + schema-on-read + Glue crawler/DynamicFrame."},{"id":"E2B-30","d":2,"ts":"2.3.1","t":"Redshift COPY parallel load","q":"Every night, an application writes 200 GB of gzip-compressed CSV data to Amazon S3 as 400 files of similar size under one prefix. A data engineer must load the data into an Amazon Redshift table as fast as possible. The cluster has 32 slices. Which approach meets this requirement?","o":["Run a single COPY command that references the prefix, so that Redshift loads the files in parallel across all slices.","Run 400 separate COPY commands at the same time, one for each file.","Use an AWS Glue job to read the files and insert rows into Redshift with JDBC INSERT statements.","Concatenate the 400 gzip files into one large gzip-compressed file, and then run one COPY command."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: '400 files of similar size', '32 slices' dan 'as fast as possible'. Satu COPY yang menunjuk ke prefix (atau manifest) membuat Redshift membagi file ke semua slice dan memuatnya secara paralel; jumlah file yang merupakan kelipatan jumlah slice dengan ukuran serupa adalah praktik terbaik. Banyak COPY bersamaan ke tabel yang sama justru diserialisasi dan lebih lambat daripada satu COPY. INSERT per baris lewat JDBC sangat lambat untuk ratusan GB. Menggabungkan semua menjadi satu file gzip menghilangkan paralelisme karena file terkompresi tidak bisa dipecah sehingga dimuat oleh satu slice (hanya file teks berdelimiter tanpa kompresi yang bisa dipindai paralel dengan scan range). Ingat: load massal ke Redshift → satu COPY, banyak file berukuran sama, kelipatan jumlah slice, terkompresi.","r":["Benar — Satu COPY atas prefix memuat banyak file paralel di semua slice, cara tercepat untuk load massal.","Salah — Banyak COPY bersamaan ke satu tabel diserialisasi dan lebih lambat daripada satu COPY.","Salah — INSERT per baris melalui JDBC jauh lebih lambat daripada COPY untuk volume besar.","Salah — Satu file gzip besar tidak bisa dipecah oleh COPY, sehingga dimuat oleh satu slice dan paralelisme hilang."],"k":"Tips ujian: load cepat ke Redshift → single COPY + banyak file berukuran sama (kelipatan slice) + kompresi."},{"id":"E4B-60","d":4,"ts":"4.5.7","t":"Hub-and-spoke governance with LF-TBAC","q":"A company is implementing a hub-and-spoke data governance framework on AWS. Business units in producer accounts keep data in their own S3 buckets, and a central governance account manages the catalog and access policies for hundreds of consumers. The governance team wants permissions to scale without creating a grant for every table and every consumer. Which TWO practices support this framework? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Producers register their data locations and share their Data Catalog resources with the central governance account, which manages access centrally with AWS Lake Formation.","Each consumer receives an IAM policy with s3:* on all producer buckets so that queries never fail.","All producer data is replicated nightly into a single S3 bucket in the governance account.","The governance team defines a central LF-Tag ontology (for example, domain and classification tags), assigns tags to resources, and grants consumers permissions on tag expressions.","Each business unit defines its own classification labels independently without a shared taxonomy."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'hub-and-spoke', data tetap di 'producer accounts', governance account 'manages the catalog and access policies', dan izin harus 'scale without creating a grant for every table and every consumer'. Dalam pola ini, producer membagikan resource Data Catalog ke akun governance (hub), yang mengelola izin secara terpusat dengan Lake Formation dan membagikannya ke consumer (spoke) tanpa menyalin data. LF-Tag-based access control (LF-TBAC) dengan taksonomi tag terpusat memungkinkan grant pada ekspresi tag, sehingga tabel baru yang diberi tag otomatis tercakup tanpa grant per tabel. Distraktor terdekat adalah replikasi data ke akun governance: sentralisasi data bertentangan dengan syarat data tetap di producer dan menambah biaya. IAM s3:* melewati governance dan melanggar least privilege. Label klasifikasi yang berbeda-beda per unit merusak konsistensi governance dan membuat tag-based grant tidak dapat diandalkan. Aturan umum: governance lintas akun yang skalabel → hub governance dengan Lake Formation + LF-TBAC dengan ontologi tag bersama.","r":["Benar — Producer membagikan katalog ke hub governance yang mengelola izin terpusat dengan Lake Formation tanpa memindahkan data.","Salah — s3:* melewati kontrol Lake Formation dan melanggar least privilege.","Salah — Replikasi ke akun pusat bertentangan dengan syarat data tetap di akun producer.","Benar — Ontologi LF-Tag terpusat dan grant berbasis ekspresi tag membuat izin skalabel.","Salah — Tanpa taksonomi bersama, governance tidak konsisten dan grant berbasis tag tidak dapat diandalkan."],"k":"Tips ujian: scalable cross-account governance → central Lake Formation hub + LF-Tag ontology (TBAC), data stays with producers."},{"id":"E1B-40","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Firehose record format conversion","q":"An application sends JSON events to Amazon Data Firehose, which delivers them to Amazon S3. The analytics team wants the data stored as Apache Parquet so that Amazon Athena queries scan less data. The company wants to avoid writing custom conversion code. Which TWO actions should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog that defines the schema of the records.","Add an AWS Lambda transformation function to Firehose that converts each record to Parquet.","Enable record format conversion in the Firehose stream with a Parquet output format that references the Glue Data Catalog table.","Change the Firehose destination to Amazon Redshift and use UNLOAD to write Parquet.","Enable Amazon Kinesis Data Streams enhanced fan-out on the source."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Penentunya adalah input berupa JSON, output yang diinginkan Parquet, dan 'avoid writing custom conversion code'. Firehose memiliki fitur record format conversion bawaan yang mengubah JSON menjadi Parquet atau ORC sebelum menulis ke S3. Fitur ini membutuhkan skema yang diambil dari tabel di AWS Glue Data Catalog, sehingga Anda perlu membuat tabel tersebut lalu mengaktifkan konversi yang mereferensikannya. Lambda transformation yang menulis Parquet adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi itu justru kode konversi kustom dan Lambda di Firehose dimaksudkan untuk transformasi record, bukan serialisasi kolumnar. Redshift + UNLOAD menambah layanan yang tidak perlu, dan enhanced fan-out tidak berkaitan dengan format. Aturan umum: JSON → Parquet/ORC pada Firehose → record format conversion + skema Glue Data Catalog.","r":["Benar — Konversi format di Firehose membutuhkan skema dari tabel Glue Data Catalog.","Salah — Membutuhkan kode konversi kustom yang ingin dihindari.","Benar — Record format conversion bawaan menulis Parquet ke S3 tanpa kode.","Salah — Menambah Redshift dan langkah UNLOAD yang tidak perlu.","Salah — Enhanced fan-out mengatur throughput konsumen, bukan format output."],"k":"Tips ujian: Firehose JSON → Parquet/ORC → record format conversion + Glue Data Catalog table (tanpa Lambda)."},{"id":"E1A-41","d":1,"ts":"1.1.6","t":"Avoiding recursive S3 triggers","q":"A Lambda function is invoked by S3 Event Notifications for every object created in a bucket. The function converts each CSV file to Parquet and writes the output back to the same bucket. After deployment, the Lambda invocations and S3 costs increase uncontrollably. What is the MOST likely cause and the best fix?","o":["The Lambda concurrency limit is too low; increase reserved concurrency.","The function's output objects trigger the same notification, creating a recursive loop; write the output to a different bucket or to a prefix that the notification filter does not match.","S3 Event Notifications deliver each event 100 times; enable S3 Versioning to stop duplicates.","The Parquet files are too large; reduce the output file size."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: Lambda dipicu oleh 'every object created' dan menulis output 'back to the same bucket', lalu invocation 'increase uncontrollably'. Ini adalah pola recursive loop klasik: objek Parquet yang ditulis Lambda memicu event ObjectCreated baru, yang memanggil Lambda lagi, dan seterusnya. Solusinya adalah menulis output ke bucket lain, atau memakai filter prefix/suffix sehingga notifikasi hanya cocok dengan input (misalnya prefix input/ dan suffix .csv), bukan output. Distraktor terdekat adalah menaikkan concurrency: justru mempercepat loop dan biaya. S3 tidak mengirim setiap event 100 kali, dan ukuran file bukan penyebabnya. Aturan umum: hindari trigger S3 yang menulis ke lokasi yang sama-sama dipantau; pisahkan bucket/prefix input dan output.","r":["Salah — Menambah concurrency justru mempercepat loop rekursif dan menaikkan biaya.","Benar — Output yang ditulis ke bucket yang sama memicu ulang fungsi; pisahkan bucket atau prefix output.","Salah — Notifikasi S3 tidak menggandakan event sebanyak itu, dan versioning tidak menghentikan loop.","Salah — Ukuran file tidak menyebabkan invocation yang terus bertambah."],"k":"Lambda menulis ke bucket yang sama dengan trigger-nya → recursive loop → pisahkan bucket/prefix output."},{"id":"E2A-53","d":2,"ts":"2.1.7","t":"Iceberg table maintenance","q":"A streaming job writes to Apache Iceberg tables stored in an S3 general purpose bucket and registered in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Each commit creates many small files, and Athena query times have tripled over several weeks. Storage costs are also increasing because old snapshots are never cleaned up. The company wants to fix both issues with the LEAST operational overhead and keep the tables where they are. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Schedule an Athena OPTIMIZE ... REWRITE DATA USING BIN_PACK and VACUUM query every hour with Amazon EventBridge Scheduler and AWS Lambda.","Enable AWS Glue Data Catalog table optimizers for compaction and snapshot retention on the Iceberg tables.","Increase the Athena workgroup data scan limit and use larger DPU capacity reservations.","Convert the tables to Hive-style Parquet and run an AWS Glue crawler every hour."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'many small files', 'old snapshots are never cleaned up', 'LEAST operational overhead', dan 'keep the tables where they are' (tetap di general purpose bucket). AWS Glue Data Catalog menyediakan table optimizer terkelola untuk tabel Iceberg: compaction menggabungkan file kecil menjadi file besar, snapshot retention menghapus snapshot lama sesuai konfigurasi, dan orphan file deletion membersihkan file yang tidak direferensikan; semuanya berjalan otomatis tanpa job yang harus ditulis. Distraktor terdekat adalah OPTIMIZE dan VACUUM di Athena yang dijadwalkan: perintahnya valid untuk Iceberg, tetapi tim harus membangun penjadwalan, menangani kegagalan, dan membayar query berulang. Menambah kapasitas Athena tidak menyelesaikan akar masalah file kecil. Kembali ke Hive Parquet menghilangkan fitur Iceberg. Aturan umum: Iceberg di general purpose bucket + pemeliharaan otomatis → Glue Data Catalog table optimizers; di table bucket → S3 Tables maintenance.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi memerlukan penjadwalan dan kode kustom sehingga overhead lebih tinggi daripada optimizer terkelola.","Benar — Optimizer Glue Data Catalog otomatis melakukan compaction dan snapshot retention pada tabel Iceberg di lokasi yang ada.","Salah — Menambah kapasitas tidak mengurangi jumlah file kecil maupun snapshot lama.","Salah — Kembali ke Hive Parquet menghilangkan ACID dan time travel serta tidak menyelesaikan masalah file kecil."],"k":"Iceberg small files + snapshot buildup, least effort → Glue Data Catalog table optimizers (compaction, snapshot retention, orphan file deletion)."},{"id":"E1C-68","d":1,"ts":"1.4.8","t":"CDK reusable constructs","q":"A platform team supports 15 data teams that all use the AWS CDK in TypeScript. Each team must create ingestion buckets with the same standards: KMS encryption, blocked public access, lifecycle rules, access logging, and an AWS Glue crawler. Teams currently copy and paste code, and the configurations have diverged. Which solution provides repeatable deployments with the LEAST ongoing effort?","o":["Write a wiki page with the required settings and ask each team to follow it.","Use AWS Config rules to detect noncompliant buckets after they are deployed.","Create a custom CDK construct that encapsulates the standard bucket and crawler configuration, publish it as a versioned package, and have teams instantiate the construct in their apps.","Give each team a copy of a CloudFormation YAML template to edit as needed."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: semua tim memakai 'same standards', konfigurasi saat ini 'diverged' karena copy-paste, dan diinginkan 'repeatable deployments with the LEAST ongoing effort'. Custom construct CDK (pola L3) membungkus resource dan default standar dalam satu komponen yang dapat digunakan ulang; dipublikasikan sebagai paket berversi, sehingga tim cukup meng-instantiate construct dan perbaikan standar menyebar melalui pembaruan versi. Distractor terdekat adalah AWS Config rules: mendeteksi ketidakpatuhan setelah deploy, tetapi tidak mencegah divergensi atau membuat deployment berulang. Wiki dan salinan template yang bisa diedit tetap menimbulkan divergensi. Aturan umum: pola infrastruktur yang dipakai ulang lintas tim di CDK → custom construct library.","r":["Salah — Dokumentasi tidak menjamin konsistensi dan tetap bergantung pada copy-paste.","Salah — Config rules hanya mendeteksi setelah deploy, tidak menyediakan komponen yang dapat dipakai ulang.","Benar — Construct berversi menyatukan standar dan menghilangkan copy-paste.","Salah — Salinan yang bisa diedit akan kembali menyimpang dari standar."],"k":"Tips ujian: reusable infrastructure pattern in CDK → custom construct (L3) package."},{"id":"E2B-18","d":2,"ts":"2.2.4","t":"Athena partition projection","q":"IoT data lands in Amazon S3 every hour under s3://iot/dt=YYYY-MM-DD/hour=HH/device_type=X/, with 12 known device types. The table is queried only by Amazon Athena. A scheduled AWS Glue crawler adds the new partitions, but queries on the latest hour often miss data until the crawler finishes, and query planning has become slow because the table has more than 500,000 partitions. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE from an AWS Lambda function every hour.","Run the crawler every 10 minutes and add a partition index on dt and hour.","Use an AWS Glue ETL job that calls BatchCreatePartition after every file is written.","Enable partition projection on the table with a date range for dt, an integer range for hour, and an enum for device_type."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'queried only by Amazon Athena', partisi baru 'miss data until the crawler finishes', 'more than 500,000 partitions' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Partition projection membuat Athena menghitung partisi dari konfigurasi properti tabel (rentang tanggal, rentang angka, enum) tanpa membaca atau menyimpan partisi di Data Catalog. Partisi jam terbaru langsung dapat di-query begitu file mendarat, dan perencanaan query lebih cepat untuk tabel dengan sangat banyak partisi. Crawler lebih sering plus partition index memang mengurangi gejala, tetapi tetap ada jeda dan biaya crawler. MSCK REPAIR tiap jam makin lambat seiring jumlah partisi bertambah. BatchCreatePartition dari job adalah kode kustom. Ingat: Athena-only + partisi sangat banyak/terprediksi + data langsung terlihat → partition projection.","r":["Salah — MSCK REPAIR memindai seluruh lokasi dan makin lambat seiring jumlah partisi; tetap ada jeda.","Salah — Crawler lebih sering menambah biaya dan tetap menyisakan jeda sebelum partisi baru terdaftar.","Salah — Memanggil API partisi dari job adalah kode kustom tambahan yang harus dipelihara.","Benar — Partition projection menghilangkan pendaftaran partisi dan mempercepat query planning khusus untuk Athena."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Athena only' + 'highly partitioned' + 'no partition management' → partition projection."},{"id":"E4A-42","d":4,"ts":"4.2.3","t":"Redshift row-level security","q":"A sales table in Amazon Redshift contains data for all regions. Regional sales managers query the table with BI tools. Each manager must see only the rows for the regions assigned to that manager in a mapping table named user_regions (username, region). Managers must not be able to bypass the restriction by writing their own SQL. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a separate view for each region and grant each manager access to the matching view.","Create a row-level security policy whose predicate allows rows where region is in the regions mapped to current_user in user_regions, attach the policy to the managers' role, and turn on row-level security for the sales table.","Add a WHERE clause on region to every dashboard in the BI tool.","Create one table per region by using CREATE TABLE AS and grant each manager access to the relevant tables."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only the rows for the regions assigned' dan 'must not be able to bypass'. Redshift row-level security (RLS) memungkinkan CREATE RLS POLICY dengan predikat, misalnya region IN (SELECT region FROM user_regions WHERE username = current_user), lalu ATTACH RLS POLICY ke tabel untuk role tertentu dan ALTER TABLE ... ROW LEVEL SECURITY ON. Filter ditegakkan oleh database pada setiap query, termasuk SQL buatan sendiri. View per region dan tabel per region berfungsi, tetapi menambah objek dan pengelolaan setiap ada perubahan mapping, dan tabel per region menduplikasi data. Filter di dashboard BI dapat dihindari dengan query langsung. Aturan umum: filter baris per pengguna yang tidak bisa dihindari di Redshift → RLS policy.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi tetapi tidak skalabel; setiap region dan perubahan mapping butuh objek dan grant baru.","Benar — RLS policy ditegakkan oleh database untuk semua query dan memakai mapping yang dinamis.","Salah — Filter di sisi BI dapat dihindari dengan menulis SQL sendiri.","Salah — Menduplikasi data dan menambah overhead pemeliharaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'users see only their rows' di Redshift → row-level security policy (CREATE/ATTACH RLS POLICY)."},{"id":"E3B-08","d":3,"ts":"3.3.1","t":"Amazon EMR logging to S3","q":"A data engineering team runs nightly Spark jobs on transient Amazon EMR on EC2 clusters that terminate automatically after the steps finish. When a step fails, engineers cannot find the step and YARN container logs because the cluster is gone. Auditors also require these logs to be retained for 1 year. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Enable termination protection so that engineers can SSH into the primary node and read /mnt/var/log after a failure.","Install the CloudWatch agent on all nodes with a bootstrap action and set the log groups to never expire.","Specify an Amazon S3 log URI when launching each cluster and apply an S3 Lifecycle rule that expires log objects after 1 year.","Enable CloudTrail data events for Amazon EMR to capture step output."],"a":[2],"e":"Persyaratannya: cluster 'transient' (log di node hilang saat terminate), log harus 'retained for 1 year', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Dengan menentukan log URI S3 saat membuat cluster, EMR secara otomatis mengarsipkan log step, YARN container, dan node ke S3 secara berkala, sehingga log tetap ada setelah cluster mati. S3 Lifecycle rule mengurus retensi 1 tahun tanpa kerja manual. Distraktor terdekat adalah CloudWatch agent via bootstrap action, yang memang bisa tetapi menambah konfigurasi agent dan biaya ingestion, serta 'never expire' tidak sesuai retensi 1 tahun. Termination protection membuat cluster tetap hidup (biaya) dan bertentangan dengan pola transient. Aturan: log EMR yang harus bertahan setelah terminate → log URI S3.","r":["Salah — Mencegah terminasi membuat biaya cluster terus berjalan dan bertentangan dengan desain transient.","Salah — Bisa bekerja tetapi menambah overhead agent dan retensi 'never expire' tidak sesuai kebutuhan 1 tahun.","Benar — EMR otomatis mengarsipkan log ke S3 log URI, dan Lifecycle rule mengatur retensi 1 tahun tanpa usaha manual.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API EMR, bukan output step atau log container."],"k":"Tips ujian: log EMR hilang setelah cluster terminate → set log URI ke S3 saat launch."},{"id":"E3A-53","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Athena CTAS to Parquet","q":"Analysts query 5 TB of gzip-compressed CSV log files in Amazon S3 through Amazon Athena. Most queries filter on event_date and select 4 of the 60 columns, and costs are high. The data engineer wants a one-time conversion of the existing data by using only Athena SQL. Which statement should the data engineer run?","o":["CREATE VIEW logs_v AS SELECT * FROM logs_csv WHERE event_date IS NOT NULL","ALTER TABLE logs_csv SET TBLPROPERTIES ('compressionType' = 'snappy')","CREATE TABLE logs_parquet WITH (format = 'PARQUET', partitioned_by = ARRAY['event_date'], external_location = 's3://bucket/logs-parquet/') AS SELECT col1, col2, ..., event_date FROM logs_csv","INSERT INTO logs_csv SELECT * FROM logs_csv WHERE event_date IS NOT NULL"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'filter on event_date', 'select 4 of 60 columns', 'costs are high', dan 'using only Athena SQL'. Athena ditagih berdasarkan data yang dipindai. Format kolumnar Parquet membuat Athena hanya membaca kolom yang dipakai, dan partisi berdasarkan event_date membuat Athena melewati partisi yang tidak relevan. CTAS dengan format = 'PARQUET' dan partitioned_by mengonversi data sekali jalan langsung dari SQL dan mendaftarkan tabel baru. Perhatikan bahwa kolom partisi harus berada di urutan terakhir dalam SELECT. View tidak mengubah format data, jadi setiap query tetap memindai CSV penuh. Mengubah properti tabel tidak mengonversi file yang sudah ada. INSERT INTO ke tabel CSV yang sama menggandakan data. Aturan umum: hemat biaya Athena → kolumnar (Parquet/ORC) + partisi + kompresi, dan CTAS adalah cara konversi tercepat dengan SQL.","r":["Salah — View tidak mengubah format; query tetap memindai seluruh CSV.","Salah — Properti tabel tidak mengonversi file yang sudah ada di S3.","Benar — CTAS menulis ulang data sebagai Parquet yang dipartisi berdasarkan event_date sehingga data yang dipindai turun drastis.","Salah — Menulis ulang ke tabel CSV yang sama menggandakan data tanpa mengubah format."],"k":"Tips ujian: konversi CSV ke Parquet + partisi hanya dengan Athena → CTAS (kolom partisi di akhir SELECT)."},{"id":"E3A-65","d":3,"ts":"3.2.6","t":"Rolling average with window functions","q":"A table daily_sales(sale_date, store_id, revenue) in Amazon Redshift has exactly one row per store per day with no missing dates. An analyst needs a 7-day rolling average of revenue for each store, where each day's value averages that day and the 6 previous days. Which expression produces the correct result?","o":["AVG(revenue) OVER (PARTITION BY store_id ORDER BY sale_date ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)","AVG(revenue) OVER (PARTITION BY store_id ORDER BY sale_date ROWS BETWEEN 7 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)","AVG(revenue) with GROUP BY store_id, DATE_TRUNC('week', sale_date)","AVG(revenue) OVER (PARTITION BY sale_date ORDER BY store_id ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)"],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya '7-day rolling average', 'for each store', dan 'that day and the 6 previous days'. Rolling (moving) average dihitung dengan fungsi window: PARTITION BY store_id memisahkan perhitungan per toko, ORDER BY sale_date mengurutkan berdasarkan waktu, dan frame ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW mencakup tepat 7 baris (hari ini ditambah 6 hari sebelumnya). Karena stem menjamin satu baris per hari tanpa tanggal yang hilang, 7 baris sama dengan 7 hari. Frame 7 PRECEDING mencakup 8 baris sehingga menjadi rata-rata 8 hari. GROUP BY minggu menghasilkan rata-rata mingguan tetap (tumbling), bukan nilai bergulir per hari, dan menghilangkan detail harian. Partisi berdasarkan tanggal dan urutan berdasarkan store_id merata-ratakan antar toko, bukan antar hari. Aturan umum: rolling average = window function dengan frame N-1 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW; jika ada tanggal yang hilang, buat date spine dulu karena ROWS menghitung baris, bukan hari.","r":["Benar — Partisi per toko, urut per tanggal, dan frame 6 PRECEDING + CURRENT ROW menghasilkan rata-rata bergulir 7 hari.","Salah — 7 PRECEDING ditambah CURRENT ROW mencakup 8 baris, sehingga menjadi rata-rata 8 hari.","Salah — GROUP BY minggu menghasilkan rata-rata mingguan tetap, bukan rolling average harian.","Salah — Partisi per tanggal merata-ratakan antar toko, bukan antar hari."],"k":"Tips ujian: rolling average N hari → AVG() OVER (PARTITION BY key ORDER BY date ROWS BETWEEN N-1 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)."},{"id":"E1C-31","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions payload limits","q":"In an AWS Step Functions workflow, an AWS Lambda function produces a 2 MB JSON summary that the next three states need. Executions fail with the error States.DataLimitExceeded. Which solution should the data engineer implement?","o":["Compress the JSON with gzip inside the Lambda function and return it as a Base64 string.","Request a service quota increase for the Step Functions payload size.","Switch to an Express workflow, which has a larger payload limit.","Have the Lambda function write the summary to Amazon S3 and return only the S3 object key, which the next states use to read the data."],"a":[3],"e":"Error 'States.DataLimitExceeded' muncul karena input/output state Step Functions dibatasi 256 KiB (kuota keras untuk Standard maupun Express). Pola yang direkomendasikan adalah menyimpan payload besar di Amazon S3 dan hanya meneruskan referensi (bucket/key) antar state; state berikutnya membaca data dari S3. Distractor terdekat adalah kompresi gzip + Base64: mungkin muat untuk sebagian data, tetapi Base64 menambah sekitar 33% ukuran dan tidak menjamin di bawah 256 KiB, serta mempersulit setiap state. Batas payload tidak bisa dinaikkan lewat kuota, dan Express memiliki batas yang sama. Aturan umum: payload besar di workflow → simpan di S3, kirim pointer.","r":["Salah — Tidak menjamin di bawah batas 256 KiB dan menambah kompleksitas di setiap state.","Salah — Batas ukuran input/output adalah kuota keras.","Salah — Express memiliki batas payload yang sama, 256 KiB.","Benar — Menyimpan data di S3 dan meneruskan key menghindari batas payload."],"k":"Tips ujian: States.DataLimitExceeded (256 KiB) → simpan di S3, kirim referensi."},{"id":"E2A-41","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Redshift materialized views","q":"An executive dashboard in Amazon Redshift runs the same query hundreds of times per day. The query joins four large tables and aggregates revenue by region and week, and it takes 45 seconds. The base tables receive new data every hour. The company wants dashboard queries to return in a few seconds with minimal maintenance. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Create a materialized view for the aggregation with AUTO REFRESH enabled, and point the dashboard at the materialized view.","Create a standard view for the aggregation and point the dashboard at the view.","Use the UNLOAD command to write the aggregation to Amazon S3 every hour and query it with Redshift Spectrum.","Increase the number of nodes in the cluster until the query takes less than 5 seconds."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah query yang sama dijalankan 'hundreds of times per day', join dan agregasi berat '45 seconds', data dasar berubah 'every hour', dan 'minimal maintenance'. Materialized view di Redshift menyimpan hasil pra-komputasi dari join dan agregasi, sehingga dashboard membaca hasil yang sudah jadi dalam hitungan detik; AUTO REFRESH membuat Redshift memperbarui view otomatis (secara inkremental bila memungkinkan) saat tabel dasar berubah. Distraktor terdekat adalah standard view: hanya menyimpan definisi query sehingga join dan agregasi tetap dihitung ulang setiap kali. Unload ke S3 menambah pipeline, dan Spectrum biasanya lebih lambat dibanding membaca hasil lokal. Menambah node mahal dan tidak menghilangkan komputasi berulang. Aturan umum: query berat yang berulang dengan data yang berubah periodik → materialized view dengan auto refresh.","r":["Benar — Materialized view menyimpan hasil pra-komputasi, dan auto refresh menjaga hasil tetap mutakhir dengan sedikit pemeliharaan.","Salah — View biasa tetap menjalankan join dan agregasi lengkap pada setiap query.","Salah — Proses unload per jam menambah pipeline dan tidak lebih cepat daripada materialized view lokal.","Salah — Menambah node mahal dan tetap menghitung ulang query berat ratusan kali sehari."],"k":"Repeated expensive aggregation → Redshift materialized view + AUTO REFRESH; standard view = no precomputation."},{"id":"E4B-42","d":4,"ts":"4.5.1","t":"Lake Formation cross-account sharing","q":"A central data lake account manages AWS Glue Data Catalog tables with AWS Lake Formation. An analytics team in another account in the same AWS Organization must query two tables with Amazon Athena, but must not see the customer_ssn column. The company wants the LEAST operational overhead and no data copies. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Add the consumer account to the S3 bucket policy and the Glue Data Catalog resource policy, and ask analysts to avoid selecting the customer_ssn column.","In the central account, use Lake Formation to grant SELECT on the two tables to the consumer account, excluding the customer_ssn column; in the consumer account, create resource links to the shared tables and grant the analyst role permissions on them.","Copy the two tables without the customer_ssn column to an S3 bucket in the consumer account every night with an AWS Glue job.","Create an IAM role in the central account that the analysts assume to query the tables directly with full access."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: akses lintas akun dengan Athena, 'must not see the customer_ssn column', 'LEAST operational overhead', dan 'no data copies'. Lake Formation mendukung cross-account grant (via AWS RAM di belakang layar) dengan column-level permission, sehingga kolom customer_ssn dapat dikecualikan. Di akun consumer, data lake administrator membuat resource link untuk tabel yang dibagikan dan memberikan izin ke role analis, lalu Athena dapat meng-query tanpa menyalin data. Distraktor terdekat adalah bucket policy + catalog resource policy: memberi akses, tetapi tidak menegakkan pembatasan kolom; 'meminta analis tidak memilih kolom' bukan kontrol keamanan. Salinan Glue setiap malam menambah pipeline, biaya, dan data basi. Role dengan akses penuh melanggar pembatasan kolom. Aturan umum: sharing data lake lintas akun dengan kontrol kolom/baris → Lake Formation cross-account grant + resource link.","r":["Salah — Kebijakan bucket dan katalog tidak menegakkan pembatasan kolom; mengandalkan kepatuhan analis tidak aman.","Benar — Grant Lake Formation lintas akun dengan pengecualian kolom dan resource link memenuhi semua syarat tanpa salinan.","Salah — Salinan malam hari menambah overhead, biaya, dan membuat data basi.","Salah — Akses penuh melalui role mengekspos kolom customer_ssn."],"k":"Tips ujian: cross-account data lake + column restriction → Lake Formation grant to account + resource link in consumer."},{"id":"E2B-07","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler custom classifiers","q":"A company ingests application logs into Amazon S3 in a proprietary text format where each line contains a timestamp, a severity level, and a free-text message separated by custom delimiters. When an AWS Glue crawler runs on the prefix, it classifies the files as UNKNOWN and creates a table with a single string column. The company wants the crawler to infer the correct columns automatically. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Increase the number of DPUs assigned to the crawler so that it can sample more files.","Change the crawler's schema change policy to 'Update the table definition in the Data Catalog'.","Convert the crawler into an AWS Glue ETL job that uses the built-in CSV classifier.","Create a custom grok classifier that matches the log format and add it to the crawler so it runs before the built-in classifiers."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'proprietary text format', 'classifies the files as UNKNOWN' dan 'infer the correct columns automatically'. Crawler menjalankan classifier kustom lebih dulu sesuai urutan, lalu classifier bawaan; jika tidak ada yang cocok, hasilnya UNKNOWN. Untuk format log kustom, solusinya adalah custom classifier bertipe grok (pola mirip regex dengan nama field) yang ditambahkan ke crawler, sehingga skema dengan kolom timestamp, severity dan message terdeteksi. Mengubah schema change policy hanya mengatur cara crawler memperbarui tabel yang ada, bukan cara mengenali format. Crawler juga tidak punya pengaturan DPU yang bisa memperbaiki klasifikasi. Rule umum: format tidak standar (log, XML khusus, JSON dengan path tertentu, CSV dengan delimiter aneh) → custom classifier.","r":["Salah — Menambah kapasitas tidak mengubah hasil klasifikasi; masalahnya adalah tidak ada classifier yang cocok.","Salah — Schema change policy mengatur update/hapus tabel, bukan inferensi skema dari format baru.","Salah — ETL job tidak mengisi Data Catalog dengan inferensi skema, dan classifier CSV bawaan tidak cocok untuk format log kustom.","Benar — Custom grok classifier mengajari crawler pola log kustom sehingga kolom terdeteksi otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: crawler hasil 'UNKNOWN' atau satu kolom string pada format kustom → custom classifier (grok/XML/JSON/CSV)."},{"id":"E1C-20","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Decoupling with SQS for resiliency","q":"Hundreds of IoT gateways send telemetry events in unpredictable bursts that can reach 20,000 events per second. Each event must be written to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database by an AWS Lambda function. During bursts the database runs out of connections and events are lost. Which solution will make the pipeline MOST resilient without losing events?","o":["Increase the RDS instance size so it accepts more connections, and keep invoking Lambda synchronously from the gateways.","Invoke the Lambda function asynchronously from the gateways so that Lambda retries failed invocations twice.","Write the events to Amazon EventBridge and set the Lambda function as a rule target.","Send the events to an Amazon SQS queue and configure the Lambda event source mapping with a maximum concurrency that the database can handle, with a dead-letter queue for failed messages."],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhan: menahan 'unpredictable bursts' tanpa 'losing events' sementara database punya batas koneksi. SQS bertindak sebagai buffer tahan lama yang memisahkan (decouple) produsen dari konsumen; event source mapping Lambda dengan pengaturan maximum concurrency membatasi jumlah fungsi yang berjalan bersamaan sesuai kemampuan database, sementara pesan menunggu dengan aman di antrean. DLQ menyimpan pesan yang terus gagal. Distractor terdekat adalah memperbesar instance RDS: menaikkan batas koneksi tetapi burst berikutnya tetap bisa melampauinya dan tidak ada buffer. Invocation asinkron hanya retry dua kali lalu event bisa dibuang, dan concurrency tetap tidak terkendali. EventBridge ke Lambda juga tidak membatasi concurrency terhadap database. Aturan umum: beban burst ke downstream yang terbatas → buffer dengan SQS + kontrol concurrency konsumen.","r":["Salah — Kapasitas lebih besar tetap bisa terlampaui saat burst dan tidak ada penyangga untuk event.","Salah — Retry asinkron terbatas, dan concurrency tidak dibatasi sehingga database tetap kebanjiran koneksi.","Salah — EventBridge tidak menyangga atau membatasi laju pemanggilan Lambda terhadap database.","Benar — SQS menyangga burst dengan tahan lama, maximum concurrency melindungi database, dan DLQ menyimpan pesan gagal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'bursty traffic' + 'downstream limited' → SQS buffer + Lambda maximum concurrency."},{"id":"E1C-06","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"MWAA Amazon provider operators","q":"A team uses Amazon MWAA to orchestrate ETL. A new DAG task must start an existing AWS Glue job and block downstream tasks until the Glue job run finishes, failing the task if the Glue job fails. The team wants to write as little custom code as possible. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Use a PythonOperator that calls the boto3 Glue client and polls GetJobRun in a while loop with time.sleep.","Use a BashOperator that runs the AWS CLI start-job-run command.","Invoke an AWS Lambda function from the DAG that starts the Glue job and returns immediately.","Use the GlueJobOperator from the Apache Airflow Amazon provider package with wait_for_completion enabled."],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhan: memulai Glue job, 'block downstream tasks until the Glue job run finishes', gagal jika job gagal, dan 'as little custom code as possible'. Paket provider Amazon untuk Airflow (sudah tersedia di MWAA) menyediakan GlueJobOperator yang memulai job dan, dengan wait_for_completion, menunggu sampai selesai serta menandai task gagal bila job gagal. Distractor terdekat adalah PythonOperator dengan polling boto3: hasilnya sama, tetapi Anda menulis dan memelihara logika polling, timeout, dan penanganan error sendiri. BashOperator dengan CLI start-job-run langsung selesai setelah job dimulai, jadi downstream tidak menunggu. Lambda yang langsung kembali juga tidak menunggu. Aturan umum: di Airflow/MWAA, gunakan operator dan sensor dari provider Amazon sebelum menulis kode kustom.","r":["Salah — Bisa bekerja tetapi merupakan kode polling kustom yang justru ingin dihindari.","Salah — Perintah CLI hanya memulai job dan task langsung sukses, sehingga downstream tidak menunggu hasil Glue job.","Salah — Lambda yang langsung kembali tidak memblokir downstream dan menambah komponen baru.","Benar — GlueJobOperator dengan wait_for_completion menunggu job selesai dan menggagalkan task bila job gagal, tanpa kode kustom."],"k":"Tips ujian: MWAA + layanan AWS → pakai operator/sensor provider Amazon (GlueJobOperator, S3KeySensor, dll.)."},{"id":"E1C-54","d":1,"ts":"1.4.3","t":"SQL window functions for deduplication","q":"A customer_updates table in Amazon Redshift contains multiple rows per customer_id, each with an updated_at timestamp. A data engineer must return only the most recent row for each customer in a single query, and the result must include all columns of that row. Which SQL approach is the MOST appropriate?","o":["SELECT customer_id, MAX(updated_at) FROM customer_updates GROUP BY customer_id","SELECT DISTINCT * FROM customer_updates ORDER BY updated_at DESC","Use ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY updated_at DESC) in a subquery or CTE and keep the rows where the row number equals 1.","SELECT * FROM customer_updates ORDER BY customer_id, updated_at DESC LIMIT 1"],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: 'only the most recent row for each customer' dan 'must include all columns'. Window function ROW_NUMBER() dengan PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY updated_at DESC memberi nomor 1 pada baris terbaru setiap customer, lalu filter row number = 1 mengembalikan satu baris lengkap per customer dalam satu query. Ini pola deduplikasi standar di Redshift, Athena, dan Spark SQL. Distractor terdekat adalah GROUP BY dengan MAX(updated_at): mendapatkan timestamp terbaru, tetapi tidak mengembalikan kolom lain tanpa join balik ke tabel. DISTINCT * tidak menghilangkan baris yang berbeda nilainya. LIMIT 1 hanya mengembalikan satu baris untuk seluruh tabel. Aturan umum: 'latest record per key' / dedup → ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY ... ORDER BY ... DESC) = 1.","r":["Salah — Hanya mengembalikan customer_id dan timestamp, bukan seluruh kolom baris terbaru.","Salah — DISTINCT tidak menghapus versi lama yang nilainya berbeda.","Benar — ROW_NUMBER per customer memilih baris terbaru dengan seluruh kolomnya.","Salah — LIMIT 1 mengembalikan satu baris untuk seluruh tabel, bukan per customer."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'latest row per key' → ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY key ORDER BY ts DESC) = 1."},{"id":"E1A-07","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"AWS Glue streaming ETL","q":"A data engineering team must read order events from an Amazon MSK topic, join them with a reference table in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, and write the results to an Amazon S3 data lake in Parquet format. Latency of a few minutes is acceptable. The team is experienced with PySpark and wants a serverless solution. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Redshift streaming ingestion from MSK and then UNLOAD the data to Amazon S3 every hour.","Create an Amazon EMR cluster on Amazon EC2 that runs a Spark Structured Streaming application.","Create an AWS Lambda function that is triggered by the MSK topic and writes each record to Amazon S3 as a Parquet file.","Create an AWS Glue streaming ETL job that reads from the MSK topic, joins the data with the catalog table, and writes Parquet files to Amazon S3."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'experienced with PySpark', 'serverless', 'join' dengan tabel Glue Data Catalog, dan latensi 'a few minutes'. AWS Glue streaming ETL berbasis Spark Structured Streaming, serverless, bisa membaca langsung dari MSK atau Kinesis, melakukan join dengan tabel katalog, dan menulis Parquet ke S3 dalam micro-batch. Distraktor terdekat adalah EMR on EC2: kemampuannya sama tetapi tidak serverless dan perlu mengelola cluster. Lambda per record menghasilkan sangat banyak file Parquet kecil dan join lebih sulit. Redshift + UNLOAD per jam melanggar toleransi latensi dan tidak efisien. Aturan umum: streaming + Spark skills + serverless = Glue streaming ETL.","r":["Salah — UNLOAD per jam melanggar toleransi latensi beberapa menit dan menambah layanan yang tidak perlu.","Salah — Bisa berfungsi, tetapi EMR on EC2 tidak serverless dan menambah pengelolaan cluster.","Salah — Menulis satu file Parquet per record menghasilkan small files problem dan join lebih rumit.","Benar — Glue streaming ETL serverless, berbasis Spark, mendukung sumber MSK, join dengan Data Catalog, dan output Parquet ke S3."],"k":"Streaming + PySpark + serverless → AWS Glue streaming ETL job."},{"id":"E1C-43","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"MWAA failure notifications","q":"An Amazon MWAA DAG loads data every hour. When any task in the DAG fails after all of its retries, the team wants an alert to be published to an existing Amazon SNS topic that includes the DAG ID, task ID, and logical date. Which solution requires the LEAST additional infrastructure?","o":["Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter for the word 'Traceback' on the worker log group with an alarm to the SNS topic.","Set an on_failure_callback in the DAG's default_args that uses the SnsHook from the Amazon provider package to publish a message built from the task context.","Run a separate DAG every 5 minutes that queries the Airflow metadata database for failed tasks.","Create a Lambda function that scrapes the Airflow web server UI for failed tasks."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: alert ke topik SNS yang ada saat task gagal 'after all of its retries', berisi 'DAG ID, task ID, and logical date', dengan infrastruktur tambahan minimal. Airflow memanggil on_failure_callback saat task benar-benar gagal (setelah retry habis), dan context callback berisi informasi DAG, task instance, serta logical date. SnsHook dari provider Amazon yang sudah tersedia di MWAA dapat mem-publish pesan tersebut ke SNS. Distractor terdekat adalah metric filter 'Traceback': dapat memicu alarm, tetapi juga memicu pada percobaan yang kemudian berhasil dan alarm tidak membawa konteks task. DAG pemantau dan scraping UI menambah komponen dan bergantung pada internal Airflow. Aturan umum: notifikasi kegagalan task Airflow → callback (on_failure_callback) + SNS hook/operator.","r":["Salah — Pola log bisa terpicu oleh percobaan yang kemudian sukses dan alarm tidak membawa DAG ID atau task ID.","Benar — on_failure_callback dijalankan setelah retry habis dan SnsHook mengirim konteks task ke SNS.","Salah — DAG pemantau menambah beban dan bergantung pada akses metadata database.","Salah — Scraping UI rapuh dan menambah infrastruktur."],"k":"Tips ujian: alert kegagalan task Airflow → on_failure_callback + SNS."},{"id":"E2C-07","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Modeling unstructured data with S3 and DynamoDB","q":"A media company keeps metadata for millions of scanned contracts. Each contract has structured metadata (contract_id, customer, signing_date, status) and a scanned PDF file that ranges from 2 MB to 40 MB. The application must look up a contract's metadata by contract_id in single-digit milliseconds and then download the PDF. Which data model is MOST appropriate?","o":["Store the metadata and the PDF bytes as a Binary attribute in the same Amazon DynamoDB item.","Store the PDF files in Amazon S3 and store the metadata plus the S3 object key in Amazon DynamoDB with contract_id as the partition key.","Store both the metadata and the PDFs as BLOB columns in an Amazon Redshift table.","Store the PDFs in Amazon EFS and use an AWS Glue crawler to build a table of metadata that the application queries with Amazon Athena."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah kombinasi data structured (metadata) dan unstructured (PDF 2–40 MB) serta kebutuhan 'single-digit milliseconds' lookup. Pola yang direkomendasikan adalah menyimpan objek besar/unstructured di Amazon S3 dan menyimpan metadata plus pointer (S3 key) di DynamoDB. DynamoDB memberikan lookup key-value berlatensi milidetik, sedangkan S3 menyimpan file besar dengan murah dan tahan lama. Item DynamoDB dibatasi 400 KB sehingga PDF 2–40 MB tidak muat. Redshift adalah data warehouse untuk analitik, bukan untuk lookup per baris berlatensi rendah atau penyimpanan file besar. Athena adalah query engine ad hoc dengan latensi detik, tidak cocok untuk lookup aplikasi. Aturan umum: unstructured/objek besar → S3; metadata yang di-query aplikasi → DynamoDB dengan pointer ke S3.","r":["Salah — Batas ukuran item DynamoDB adalah 400 KB, sehingga PDF 2–40 MB tidak bisa disimpan dalam item.","Benar — S3 menyimpan PDF besar dengan murah, dan DynamoDB memberikan lookup metadata milidetik beserta S3 key.","Salah — Redshift ditujukan untuk analitik kolumnar, bukan lookup baris berlatensi rendah atau penyimpanan file besar.","Salah — Athena memiliki latensi query beberapa detik dan tidak cocok untuk lookup aplikasi milidetik."],"k":"Tips ujian: file besar/unstructured → S3, metadata + pointer → DynamoDB (ingat batas item 400 KB)."},{"id":"E4A-32","d":4,"ts":"4.2.1","t":"Athena workgroup IAM policies","q":"A company has several Amazon Athena workgroups. The workgroup 'analysts' enforces a query result location, encryption, and a per-query data scan limit. The security team requires that analysts run queries only in the 'analysts' workgroup and cannot switch to the 'primary' workgroup, which has no limits. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Attach the AWS managed policy AmazonAthenaFullAccess to the analysts' IAM role.","Enable the 'override client-side settings' option on the 'primary' workgroup.","Create a custom IAM policy that allows athena:StartQueryExecution, athena:GetQueryExecution, and athena:GetQueryResults only on the ARN of the 'analysts' workgroup.","Delete the 'primary' workgroup so that analysts must use the 'analysts' workgroup."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only in the analysts workgroup' dan 'cannot switch'. Athena workgroup adalah resource IAM dengan ARN arn:aws:athena:region:account:workgroup/nama, sehingga custom IAM policy dapat membatasi aksi query hanya pada workgroup tertentu. Dengan begitu kontrol biaya dan enkripsi yang ditegakkan workgroup tidak dapat dihindari. AmazonAthenaFullAccess mengizinkan semua workgroup. Opsi override client-side settings hanya memaksa setting workgroup kepada query di workgroup itu, bukan mencegah pengguna memakai workgroup lain. Workgroup 'primary' tidak bisa dihapus. Aturan umum: pembatasan akses Athena per tim → IAM policy pada ARN workgroup.","r":["Salah — Managed policy ini memberi akses ke semua workgroup sehingga analis bisa berpindah ke 'primary'.","Salah — Override setting hanya berlaku pada workgroup itu dan tidak mencegah analis memakai workgroup lain.","Benar — Membatasi aksi Athena ke ARN workgroup 'analysts' memastikan semua query mengikuti batasan workgroup tersebut.","Salah — Workgroup 'primary' tidak dapat dihapus."],"k":"Tips ujian: paksa tim memakai workgroup Athena tertentu → custom IAM policy dengan Resource = ARN workgroup."},{"id":"E4A-55","d":4,"ts":"4.2.5","t":"Choosing RBAC vs ABAC","q":"A company currently creates a new IAM role and policy for each data project to control access to Amazon S3 prefixes, AWS Glue jobs, and Amazon Athena workgroups. The number of projects has grown to 200, with new projects every week, and the security team is struggling with the number of roles and policies to maintain. Which authorization strategy should the company adopt to address this business need?","o":["Continue role-based access control but merge all projects into one role with access to all project resources.","Adopt attribute-based access control by tagging principals and resources with a project tag and using a small number of policies that compare the tags.","Switch to S3 object ACLs to control access to each project's data.","Create an IAM user for each project and share the credentials with the project team."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: '200 projects', 'new projects every week', dan beban 'number of roles and policies'. Ini adalah masalah klasik role explosion pada RBAC. ABAC menyelesaikannya dengan memakai tag pada principal dan resource: policy yang sama berlaku untuk semua project, dan project baru hanya membutuhkan tag yang tepat, bukan role atau policy baru. Menggabungkan semua project ke satu role mengurangi jumlah role tetapi menghilangkan isolasi antar project. ACL S3 hanya mencakup S3, sulit dikelola, dan direkomendasikan untuk dinonaktifkan. IAM user yang dibagikan menimbulkan credential jangka panjang dan hilangnya akuntabilitas. Aturan umum: jumlah resource/tim tumbuh cepat → ABAC; jumlah peran stabil → RBAC.","r":["Salah — Satu role untuk semua project menghapus isolasi dan melanggar least privilege.","Benar — ABAC menskalakan otorisasi dengan tag sehingga tidak perlu role dan policy baru untuk setiap project.","Salah — ACL hanya berlaku untuk S3 dan tidak mendukung kontrol yang fleksibel.","Salah — Credential bersama tidak aman dan tidak dapat diaudit per orang."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'role explosion', banyak project yang terus bertambah → ABAC."},{"id":"E4A-08","d":4,"ts":"4.1.2","t":"Interface endpoint private DNS","q":"A company creates an interface VPC endpoint for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams so that producer applications on Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets send records privately. After deployment, VPC Flow Logs show that the producers still send traffic to the public Kinesis endpoint through the NAT gateway. The producers use the default regional Kinesis endpoint in the AWS SDK. What is the MOST likely way to fix this without changing application code?","o":["Add a route for the Kinesis prefix list to the endpoint in the private subnets' route tables.","Change the endpoint type from interface to gateway so that routing is automatic.","Enable private DNS for the interface endpoint, and make sure that the VPC has DNS resolution and DNS hostnames enabled.","Attach an endpoint policy that denies all requests that do not come from the VPC."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'without changing application code' dan SDK memakai 'default regional endpoint'. Interface endpoint bekerja lewat DNS, bukan route table: endpoint mendapat nama DNS khusus, dan hanya jika private DNS diaktifkan nama default seperti kinesis.<region>.amazonaws.com akan resolve ke IP privat ENI endpoint. Private DNS mensyaratkan atribut VPC enableDnsSupport dan enableDnsHostnames bernilai true. Menambah route ke prefix list hanya berlaku untuk gateway endpoint, dan Kinesis Data Streams tidak punya gateway endpoint. Endpoint policy hanya membatasi request yang melewati endpoint; request yang tidak melewati endpoint tidak terpengaruh. Aturan umum: interface endpoint tidak dipakai otomatis tanpa private DNS (atau mengganti endpoint URL di kode).","r":["Salah — Prefix list dan route table adalah mekanisme gateway endpoint, bukan interface endpoint.","Salah — Kinesis Data Streams tidak mendukung gateway endpoint; hanya S3 dan DynamoDB.","Benar — Private DNS membuat nama endpoint default resolve ke IP privat interface endpoint sehingga SDK otomatis memakai jalur privat.","Salah — Endpoint policy tidak mengubah jalur DNS; traffic tetap ke endpoint publik melalui NAT."],"k":"Tips ujian: interface endpoint tidak dipakai padahal sudah dibuat → cek private DNS + enableDnsSupport/enableDnsHostnames."},{"id":"E1C-41","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"SNS to encrypted SQS permissions","q":"An Amazon SNS topic delivers pipeline alerts to an Amazon SQS queue that is encrypted with server-side encryption using AWS KMS. After encryption was enabled with the AWS managed key for Amazon SQS (aws/sqs), messages stopped arriving in the queue. Which combination of actions will restore delivery? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Re-encrypt the queue with a customer managed KMS key whose key policy allows the sns.amazonaws.com service principal to use kms:GenerateDataKey and kms:Decrypt.","Enable raw message delivery on the SNS subscription.","Ensure the SQS queue policy allows the SNS topic ARN to perform sqs:SendMessage on the queue.","Convert the queue to an SQS FIFO queue.","Attach an IAM policy with sqs:SendMessage to the IAM user who created the topic."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Masalahnya: setelah antrean dienkripsi dengan 'AWS managed key for Amazon SQS', SNS tidak bisa mengirim. Key policy kunci AWS managed tidak bisa diubah, sehingga layanan SNS tidak diizinkan memakai kunci tersebut; solusinya memakai customer managed key yang key policy-nya mengizinkan principal sns.amazonaws.com melakukan kms:GenerateDataKey dan kms:Decrypt. Selain itu, queue policy SQS harus mengizinkan topik SNS (berdasarkan aws:SourceArn) melakukan sqs:SendMessage. Distractor terdekat adalah memberi izin kepada IAM user pembuat topik: pengiriman dilakukan oleh layanan SNS, bukan oleh user, jadi izin user tidak berpengaruh. Raw message delivery hanya mengubah format pesan, dan FIFO tidak terkait masalah enkripsi. Aturan umum: layanan AWS yang menulis ke resource terenkripsi KMS memerlukan izin di key policy customer managed key + resource policy tujuan.","r":["Benar — Customer managed key memungkinkan key policy mengizinkan SNS memakai kunci untuk mengenkripsi pesan ke antrean.","Salah — Raw delivery hanya mengubah format isi pesan, bukan izin enkripsi.","Benar — Queue policy harus mengizinkan topik SNS mengirim pesan ke antrean.","Salah — Jenis antrean tidak memengaruhi izin KMS.","Salah — Pengiriman dilakukan oleh layanan SNS, bukan oleh IAM user pembuat topik."],"k":"Tips ujian: SNS → SQS terenkripsi KMS gagal → pakai customer managed key + key policy untuk sns.amazonaws.com."},{"id":"E2A-30","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Storage platforms: EFS vs EBS vs S3","q":"A data science team runs preprocessing scripts on 20 Amazon EC2 instances across two Availability Zones. All instances must read and write the same set of files concurrently through a standard POSIX file system interface, and capacity must grow automatically as files are added. Which storage service should a data engineer choose?","o":["An Amazon EBS gp3 volume attached to one instance and shared through NFS","Amazon EC2 instance store volumes on each instance","Amazon S3 accessed through the AWS CLI","Amazon EFS"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah '20 Amazon EC2 instances across two Availability Zones', 'read and write the same set of files concurrently', 'POSIX file system interface', dan 'grow automatically'. Amazon EFS adalah file system NFS fully managed yang dapat di-mount bersamaan oleh banyak instance di beberapa AZ, mendukung semantik POSIX, dan kapasitasnya elastis tanpa provisioning. Distraktor terdekat adalah EBS yang dibagikan via NFS dari satu instance: bisa jalan, tetapi menciptakan single point of failure, terikat satu AZ, dan kapasitas tidak tumbuh otomatis. Instance store bersifat lokal dan ephemeral, sehingga tidak bisa dibagikan. S3 adalah object storage, bukan file system POSIX. Aturan umum: shared POSIX file system lintas instance/AZ dengan kapasitas elastis → Amazon EFS; block storage satu instance → EBS; object → S3.","r":["Salah — EBS terikat pada satu AZ dan satu instance server NFS menjadi single point of failure serta kapasitasnya tidak otomatis bertambah.","Salah — Instance store bersifat lokal dan ephemeral, tidak dapat diakses bersama oleh instance lain.","Salah — S3 adalah object storage tanpa semantik POSIX seperti file locking dan append.","Benar — EFS menyediakan file system POSIX bersama lintas AZ dengan kapasitas elastis otomatis."],"k":"Shared POSIX file system, multi-AZ, auto-growing → Amazon EFS."},{"id":"E2B-54","d":2,"ts":"2.3.5","t":"CloudWatch Logs retention","q":"AWS Glue jobs and AWS Lambda functions in a data pipeline write logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An audit found that some log lines contain customer email addresses. The company policy says that such operational logs must be kept for no longer than 30 days. Which solution meets the retention requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Export the log groups to Amazon S3 every day and delete the log groups each month.","Set the retention setting of the relevant CloudWatch Logs log groups to 30 days.","Schedule a Lambda function that calls DeleteLogStream for streams older than 30 days.","Create a metric filter that removes email addresses from the logs after 30 days."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: logs 'must be kept for no longer than 30 days' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. CloudWatch Logs punya setting retensi per log group; secara default log disimpan selamanya (Never expire). Mengatur retensi ke 30 hari membuat CloudWatch Logs menghapus event yang lebih lama secara otomatis. Mengekspor ke S3 justru membuat salinan data PII di tempat lain dan menambah pekerjaan. Lambda yang menghapus log stream adalah kode kustom untuk fitur yang sudah tersedia. Metric filter hanya membuat metrik dari pola log, tidak mengubah atau menghapus data. Ingat: 'retain logs for N days' → retensi log group CloudWatch Logs (default: never expire).","r":["Salah — Ekspor membuat salinan PII tambahan dan menambah proses manual.","Benar — Retensi log group menghapus event log yang lebih lama dari 30 hari secara otomatis.","Salah — Lambda kustom menambah kode dan penjadwalan untuk fungsi yang sudah tersedia secara native.","Salah — Metric filter tidak mengubah atau menghapus isi log."],"k":"Tips ujian: CloudWatch Logs default never expire → set log group retention untuk memenuhi kebijakan."},{"id":"E3B-55","d":3,"ts":"3.4.3","t":"AWS DMS data validation","q":"A company used AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to perform a full load plus ongoing change data capture from an on-premises Oracle database to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. Before cutover, the data engineer must verify that the rows in the target are consistent with the source and identify any mismatched rows. Which solution meets this requirement with the LEAST effort?","o":["Enable data validation on the AWS DMS task and review the validation state and the failed rows recorded by DMS.","Export both databases to CSV and compare the files with a custom script.","Compare the table row counts in the DMS task statistics only.","Run an AWS Glue crawler on both databases and compare the schemas."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'verify that the rows in the target are consistent with the source' dan 'identify any mismatched rows'. AWS DMS data validation membandingkan data baris per baris antara sumber dan target selama full load dan CDC, menampilkan status validasi per tabel, dan mencatat baris yang gagal validasi (di tabel kontrol awsdms_validation_failures_v1 pada target; untuk target PostgreSQL dengan DMS 3.6.1 ke atas tersedia juga awsdms_validation_failures_v2). Distraktor terdekat adalah membandingkan row count di statistik task: jumlah baris bisa sama walaupun nilai kolom berbeda, jadi tidak membuktikan konsistensi isi. Ekspor CSV dan script kustom membutuhkan banyak usaha. Crawler hanya membandingkan skema. Aturan: konsistensi sumber-target saat migrasi DMS → DMS data validation.","r":["Benar — DMS validation membandingkan isi baris sumber dan target serta mencatat baris yang tidak cocok.","Salah — Ekspor dan script kustom membutuhkan usaha besar dan rawan kesalahan.","Salah — Jumlah baris yang sama tidak menjamin nilai di setiap baris konsisten.","Salah — Perbandingan skema tidak mendeteksi perbedaan isi data."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'verify source and target data match' pada migrasi DMS → enable DMS data validation."},{"id":"E2C-18","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Redshift ALTER COLUMN for VARCHAR growth","q":"A column named product_desc in an Amazon Redshift table is defined as VARCHAR(100). The source system has started sending descriptions of up to 400 characters, and the nightly COPY now fails with a length error. The column uses LZO encoding and has no default value or key constraints. The table has 2 billion rows and must remain available to queries. Which solution meets the requirement with the LEAST effort?","o":["Run ALTER TABLE ... ALTER COLUMN product_desc TYPE VARCHAR(500).","Create a new table with the larger column, INSERT INTO ... SELECT all rows, and swap the table names.","Add the TRUNCATECOLUMNS option to the COPY command so that long values are cut to 100 characters.","Change the column to the SUPER data type."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah perubahan karakteristik data (panjang string bertambah) dengan 'LEAST effort' dan tabel harus tetap tersedia. Amazon Redshift mendukung ALTER TABLE ... ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE untuk mengubah ukuran kolom VARCHAR (memperbesar, atau memperkecil asal tidak di bawah panjang data terpanjang yang ada), sehingga perubahan dilakukan langsung tanpa deep copy manual. Batasannya: tidak bisa untuk kolom dengan encoding BYTEDICT, RUNLENGTH, TEXT255, atau TEXT32K, kolom dengan default value, kolom dengan constraint UNIQUE/PRIMARY KEY/FOREIGN KEY, dan tidak bisa di dalam transaction block. Deep copy ke tabel baru dan rename juga berhasil, tetapi lebih banyak langkah dan memakan waktu untuk 2 miliar baris. TRUNCATECOLUMNS membuat COPY berhasil tetapi memotong data sehingga deskripsi menjadi tidak lengkap, yang merupakan kehilangan data. SUPER ditujukan untuk data semi-structured dan tidak perlu untuk string biasa. Aturan umum: VARCHAR terlalu kecil di Redshift → ALTER COLUMN TYPE untuk mengubah panjang VARCHAR; perubahan ke tipe data lain tidak didukung klausa ini dan biasanya perlu kolom baru atau deep copy.","r":["Benar — Redshift mengizinkan mengubah (di sini memperbesar) panjang VARCHAR dengan ALTER COLUMN TYPE secara langsung, dan kolom ini memenuhi syaratnya (encoding LZO, tanpa default value, tanpa constraint).","Salah — Deep copy berhasil tetapi jauh lebih banyak usaha dan waktu dibanding ALTER COLUMN.","Salah — TRUNCATECOLUMNS memotong deskripsi sehingga terjadi kehilangan data.","Salah — SUPER untuk data semi-structured; mengubah tipe ini tidak perlu dan memperumit query."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift VARCHAR kepanjangan → ALTER TABLE ... ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE VARCHAR(n) (hanya untuk ukuran VARCHAR; tidak untuk encoding BYTEDICT/RUNLENGTH/TEXT255/TEXT32K, kolom ber-default, atau ber-constraint)."},{"id":"E4B-19","d":4,"ts":"4.3.4","t":"Redshift SSL enforcement","q":"A company's BI tools connect to an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster over JDBC. A new policy requires that all client connections to the cluster be encrypted in transit, and unencrypted connections must be rejected. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Set the require_ssl parameter to true in a custom parameter group associated with the cluster, and configure the clients to connect with SSL.","Restrict the cluster security group to allow inbound traffic only from the BI tools' IP addresses.","Enable encryption at rest on the cluster with a customer managed AWS KMS key.","Enable enhanced VPC routing on the cluster."],"a":[0],"e":"Requirement yang menentukan: koneksi klien 'encrypted in transit' dan koneksi tanpa enkripsi 'must be rejected'. Pada Amazon Redshift, parameter require_ssl = true di parameter group membuat cluster menolak koneksi yang tidak memakai SSL/TLS; klien JDBC/ODBC lalu dikonfigurasi memakai SSL. Distraktor terdekat adalah membatasi security group: ini mengontrol siapa yang boleh terhubung, tetapi trafik tetap bisa tidak terenkripsi. Enkripsi at rest dengan KMS tidak berpengaruh pada jalur koneksi. Enhanced VPC routing memaksa trafik COPY/UNLOAD melewati VPC Anda, bukan mengenkripsi koneksi klien. Aturan umum: paksa SSL ke Redshift → require_ssl di parameter group (RDS PostgreSQL: rds.force_ssl).","r":["Benar — require_ssl menolak koneksi non-SSL sehingga semua koneksi klien terenkripsi.","Salah — Security group membatasi sumber koneksi tetapi tidak memaksa enkripsi.","Salah — Enkripsi at rest tidak mengenkripsi data saat dikirim antara klien dan cluster.","Salah — Enhanced VPC routing mengatur jalur trafik COPY/UNLOAD, bukan enkripsi koneksi klien."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift 'reject unencrypted connections' → require_ssl=true."},{"id":"E4A-20","d":4,"ts":"4.1.5","t":"AWS PrivateLink endpoint services","q":"A central data team in account A runs an ingestion service behind a Network Load Balancer. Forty business-unit VPCs in other AWS accounts must send data to this service privately. Several of these VPCs use overlapping CIDR ranges, and the central team wants to control which accounts can connect. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create VPC peering connections between account A's VPC and each business-unit VPC.","Attach all VPCs to an AWS Transit Gateway and add routes to the ingestion service subnets.","Expose the ingestion service through a public Application Load Balancer protected by AWS WAF IP allow lists.","Create a VPC endpoint service (AWS PrivateLink) for the Network Load Balancer, add the business-unit accounts as allowed principals, and have each VPC create an interface endpoint."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'overlapping CIDR ranges', 'privately', dan 'control which accounts can connect'. AWS PrivateLink mengekspos service di belakang NLB sebagai endpoint service; konsumen membuat interface endpoint di VPC mereka sendiri sehingga traffic tetap privat dan tidak perlu routing antar-VPC. Karena tidak ada routing antar jaringan, CIDR yang tumpang tindih tidak menjadi masalah. Penyedia mengontrol akses dengan daftar allowed principals dan dapat mewajibkan acceptance untuk setiap koneksi. VPC peering dan Transit Gateway membutuhkan CIDR yang tidak overlap dan membuka konektivitas jaringan yang lebih luas. ALB publik melanggar syarat privat. Aturan umum: expose satu service ke banyak VPC/akun, terutama dengan CIDR overlap → PrivateLink.","r":["Salah — Peering tidak mendukung CIDR yang tumpang tindih dan 40 peering sulit dikelola.","Salah — Transit Gateway juga membutuhkan CIDR yang tidak overlap untuk routing dan membuka akses jaringan lebih luas.","Salah — Endpoint publik melanggar syarat koneksi privat.","Benar — PrivateLink menghubungkan konsumen secara privat tanpa routing, mendukung CIDR overlap, dan dikontrol lewat allowed principals."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'overlapping CIDR' + 'expose service privately to many accounts' → AWS PrivateLink (endpoint service + NLB)."},{"id":"E3B-19","d":3,"ts":"3.3.3","t":"CloudWatch composite alarms","q":"A streaming pipeline sends too many false alerts. The team wants to be paged only when BOTH the AWS Lambda processor's error count alarm is in ALARM state AND the dead-letter queue's ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible alarm is in ALARM state at the same time. The solution should use native features with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Increase the evaluation periods of both existing alarms so that they trigger less often.","Create a CloudWatch composite alarm with a rule expression that combines both alarms with AND, and send only the composite alarm's notifications to the paging SNS topic.","Subscribe a Lambda function to both alarms that stores alarm states in Amazon DynamoDB and pages when both are active.","Create an EventBridge Scheduler schedule that checks both metrics every minute."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'only when BOTH ... at the same time' dan 'native features with the LEAST operational overhead'. CloudWatch composite alarm mengevaluasi status beberapa alarm dengan ekspresi logika (AND, OR, NOT), sehingga notifikasi hanya dikirim saat kedua kondisi terpenuhi; alarm anak bisa dibiarkan tanpa action agar tidak ada noise. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda yang menyimpan status di DynamoDB — hasilnya sama, tetapi berupa kode kustom yang perlu dirawat. Menambah evaluation periods hanya memperlambat alarm individu, tidak menggabungkan kondisi. Aturan: kurangi alarm noise dengan menggabungkan kondisi → composite alarm.","r":["Salah — Hanya menunda alarm masing-masing, tidak mensyaratkan kedua kondisi terjadi bersamaan.","Benar — Composite alarm dengan AND mengirim page hanya saat kedua alarm aktif, tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Logika kustom dengan Lambda dan DynamoDB menambah overhead pengembangan dan perawatan.","Salah — Scheduler bukan mekanisme evaluasi alarm dan tetap butuh logika kustom."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'alert only when alarm A AND alarm B' / 'reduce alarm noise' → CloudWatch composite alarm."},{"id":"E1A-64","d":1,"ts":"1.1.11","t":"Kinesis retention and replay","q":"A bug in a stream-processing application that consumes an Amazon Kinesis data stream corrupted the output for the last 3 days. The bug is now fixed, and the team must reprocess the original records from the past 3 days. The stream currently uses the default retention period. What should the data engineer have configured to make this possible, and how should reprocessing be done?","o":["Enable server-side encryption so that records are stored durably for replay.","Keep the default retention period and restart the consumer with a LATEST shard iterator.","Increase the stream retention period beyond 3 days in advance, and restart the consumer with a shard iterator of type AT_TIMESTAMP set to the time when the bug was introduced.","Increase the number of shards so that older records are retained longer."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: harus 'reprocess the original records from the past 3 days', sedangkan stream memakai 'default retention period'. Retensi default Kinesis Data Streams adalah 24 jam, sehingga record berusia 3 hari sudah tidak ada; untuk bisa replay, retensi harus diperpanjang sebelumnya (hingga 7 hari untuk extended, atau hingga 365 hari untuk long-term retention). Setelah itu, consumer dapat membaca ulang mulai dari waktu tertentu dengan shard iterator AT_TIMESTAMP (atau TRIM_HORIZON untuk dari awal). Distraktor terdekat adalah iterator LATEST: hanya membaca record baru sehingga tidak ada replay. Enkripsi dan jumlah shard tidak memengaruhi berapa lama data disimpan. Aturan umum: replayability Kinesis = retensi yang cukup + shard iterator AT_TIMESTAMP/TRIM_HORIZON; selain itu simpan salinan mentah di S3 untuk replay jangka panjang.","r":["Salah — Enkripsi tidak memperpanjang lama penyimpanan record.","Salah — Retensi default 24 jam tidak menyimpan data 3 hari, dan LATEST hanya membaca record baru.","Benar — Retensi yang lebih panjang menyimpan record, dan AT_TIMESTAMP memulai pembacaan ulang dari waktu yang diinginkan.","Salah — Jumlah shard memengaruhi throughput, bukan retensi."],"k":"Replay Kinesis → retensi > 24 jam (hingga 365 hari) + shard iterator AT_TIMESTAMP / TRIM_HORIZON."},{"id":"E1B-30","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Glue DynamicFrame resolveChoice","q":"A data engineer builds an AWS Glue ETL job that combines product data from two sources. In one source the price column is a string, and in the other source it is a double. The AWS Glue crawler records the column as a choice type, and downstream Parquet writes fail with type errors. The engineer wants to keep all records and use a numeric price. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Delete the records whose price column is a string before the job runs.","Rewrite the job to use Apache Spark DataFrames only and infer the schema from the first file.","Use the resolveChoice transform on the DynamicFrame to cast the price column to double.","Create two separate Glue Data Catalog tables and two separate output datasets."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah kolom yang dicatat sebagai 'choice type' karena tipe berbeda di dua sumber, kebutuhan 'keep all records', dan ingin harga numerik. Glue DynamicFrame dirancang menangani skema yang tidak konsisten: transform resolveChoice dapat melakukan cast kolom ke tipe tertentu (misalnya cast:double) sehingga semua record tetap dipertahankan dengan tipe yang seragam. Menghapus record bertipe string melanggar syarat menyimpan semua record. DataFrame Spark dengan inferensi dari file pertama justru dapat gagal atau salah membaca sumber lainnya. Memisahkan tabel dan output tidak menghasilkan dataset gabungan yang diminta. Aturan umum: skema tidak konsisten antar sumber di Glue → DynamicFrame + resolveChoice.","r":["Salah — Membuang data dan melanggar syarat menyimpan semua record.","Salah — Inferensi skema dari file pertama tidak menangani tipe yang berbeda dengan andal.","Benar — resolveChoice melakukan cast kolom choice ke double sehingga semua record bisa ditulis.","Salah — Tidak menghasilkan dataset terintegrasi dan menambah kompleksitas."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'choice type / ambiguous column type in Glue' → DynamicFrame resolveChoice (cast, make_cols, make_struct)."},{"id":"E2C-44","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Bedrock knowledge base metadata filtering","q":"A company's Amazon Bedrock knowledge base contains HR documents from 30 countries in a single Amazon S3 data source. Users must receive answers only from documents for their own country and from the current policy year. The data engineer wants to implement this with the LEAST effort. Which TWO actions should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a .metadata.json file for each document in Amazon S3 with attributes such as country and policy_year, and sync the data source.","Create a separate knowledge base and vector store for each country and year combination.","Pass a metadata filter on country and policy_year in the Retrieve or RetrieveAndGenerate request for each user.","Add the country name to the beginning of every user question and rely on semantic similarity.","Fine-tune the embeddings model separately for each country."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah membatasi hasil retrieval berdasarkan atribut dokumen (negara dan tahun) dengan 'LEAST effort'. Amazon Bedrock knowledge base mendukung metadata pada data source S3 melalui file <namafile>.metadata.json di lokasi yang sama dengan dokumen; atribut tersebut ikut disimpan bersama vektor saat sinkronisasi. Saat query, aplikasi mengirim metadata filter (misalnya country equals ID dan policy_year equals 2026) pada Retrieve atau RetrieveAndGenerate sehingga hanya chunk yang cocok yang dicari. Membuat knowledge base terpisah untuk setiap kombinasi menambah banyak resource dan biaya. Menambahkan nama negara ke pertanyaan hanya memengaruhi kemiripan, bukan filter yang pasti. Fine-tuning embeddings per negara mahal dan tidak menjamin pembatasan dokumen. Aturan umum: batasi retrieval berdasarkan atribut → metadata + metadata filtering, bukan memecah knowledge base.","r":["Benar — File .metadata.json menyimpan atribut dokumen bersama vektor sehingga bisa difilter.","Salah — Knowledge base per kombinasi negara dan tahun menimbulkan ratusan resource dan overhead besar.","Benar — Metadata filter pada request retrieval membatasi hasil hanya pada dokumen negara dan tahun yang sesuai.","Salah — Teks tambahan di pertanyaan hanya memengaruhi kemiripan dan tidak menjamin pembatasan.","Salah — Fine-tuning per negara mahal dan tidak memberikan filter yang deterministik."],"k":"Tips ujian: knowledge base + batasi hasil per atribut → .metadata.json + metadata filtering saat Retrieve."},{"id":"E4B-54","d":4,"ts":"4.5.5","t":"Data sovereignty with cross-Region sharing","q":"A company runs its Amazon Redshift data warehouse in eu-central-1. A BI team in the United States wants to use Redshift cross-Region data sharing to query the data from a Redshift Serverless workgroup in us-east-1. Data sovereignty rules require that personal data of EU customers never leave the EU, but aggregated, non-personal metrics may be shared globally. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Share the full customer schema through a cross-Region datashare and apply dynamic data masking to the personal data columns for the BI team.","Create aggregated tables or materialized views that contain no personal data, add only those objects to a datashare, and share it with the us-east-1 namespace.","Share the full customer schema through a cross-Region datashare after encrypting the producer cluster with a customer managed KMS key.","Copy the full customer tables to an S3 bucket in us-east-1 and query them with Redshift Spectrum."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'personal data of EU customers never leave the EU', sementara 'aggregated, non-personal metrics may be shared globally'. Pada cross-Region data sharing, data yang di-query oleh consumer dikirim ke Region consumer, sehingga satu-satunya cara aman adalah memastikan datashare hanya berisi objek tanpa data personal, misalnya tabel agregat atau materialized view. Pola ini memenuhi kebutuhan BI sekaligus menjaga kedaulatan data. Distraktor terdekat adalah dynamic data masking: kolom ter-masking saat ditampilkan, tetapi skema lengkap tetap dibagikan dan kesalahan policy dapat mengekspos data personal ke Region lain, sehingga tidak memenuhi 'never leave'. Enkripsi KMS melindungi data at rest, tetapi data tetap diproses di us-east-1. Menyalin tabel lengkap ke S3 us-east-1 jelas memindahkan data personal keluar EU. Aturan umum: berbagi lintas yurisdiksi → minimalkan data (agregasi/anonimisasi) sebelum berbagi.","r":["Salah — Skema lengkap tetap dibagikan lintas Region; masking tidak menjamin data personal tidak meninggalkan EU.","Benar — Hanya objek agregat tanpa data personal yang dibagikan ke Region AS.","Salah — Enkripsi at rest tidak mencegah data personal diproses di us-east-1.","Salah — Menyalin tabel lengkap ke us-east-1 memindahkan data personal keluar EU."],"k":"Tips ujian: sovereignty + cross-Region sharing → share only aggregated/anonymized data; masking/encryption ≠ residency."},{"id":"E2C-29","d":2,"ts":"2.4.4","t":"OpenLineage integration with SageMaker Catalog","q":"A data platform team runs Apache Spark jobs on Amazon EMR orchestrated by Amazon MWAA, plus dbt models on Amazon Redshift. The company has adopted Amazon SageMaker Catalog as its business catalog and wants lineage from these tools to appear alongside lineage captured from AWS Glue. Which approach should the data engineer use?","o":["Emit OpenLineage-compatible lineage events from the Spark and dbt runs and send them to SageMaker Catalog by using its lineage API or the OpenLineage transport for Amazon DataZone.","Export Spark event logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and create a CloudWatch dashboard of job names.","Re-implement all Spark and dbt jobs as AWS Glue crawlers.","Store a JSON file describing each job's inputs and outputs in Amazon S3 for analysts to download."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah lineage dari tool non-Glue (Spark di EMR, Airflow/MWAA, dbt) yang harus muncul di SageMaker Catalog bersama lineage lain. Lineage SageMaker Catalog dibangun di atas standar OpenLineage, sehingga tool yang dapat menghasilkan event OpenLineage dapat mengirimkan event tersebut melalui API lineage (PostLineageEvent) atau transport OpenLineage untuk Amazon DataZone, lalu graph lineage tergabung di katalog. Dashboard CloudWatch hanya menampilkan metrik/log job, bukan hubungan dataset input-output. Crawler hanya menemukan schema dan tidak menggantikan logika transformasi Spark/dbt. File JSON di S3 tidak terintegrasi ke katalog dan tidak bisa divisualisasikan sebagai graph. Aturan umum: lineage dari tool kustom/open source ke SageMaker Catalog → kirim event OpenLineage.","r":["Benar — Event OpenLineage dari Spark/dbt dapat dikirim ke SageMaker Catalog sehingga lineage tergabung dengan lineage Glue.","Salah — Dashboard CloudWatch tidak menyajikan graph lineage dataset.","Salah — Crawler tidak menjalankan transformasi dan tidak bisa menggantikan job Spark/dbt.","Salah — File JSON di S3 tidak terintegrasi ke katalog dan tidak divisualisasikan."],"k":"Tips ujian: lineage dari Spark/Airflow/dbt ke SageMaker Catalog → OpenLineage events."},{"id":"E1C-77","d":1,"ts":"1.4.10","t":"Splittable formats and parallelism","q":"A vendor delivers a single 500 GB gzip-compressed CSV file each night to Amazon S3. An AWS Glue Spark job with 50 workers reads the file, but the Spark UI shows that the read stage runs as a single task on one executor while the other workers are idle. What is the reason, and which change will improve parallelism the MOST?","o":["The Glue job has too few workers; increase the number of workers to 100.","Gzip files are not splittable, so one task must read the whole file; ask the vendor to deliver many smaller files or use a splittable format such as Parquet or bzip2-compressed CSV.","Spark cannot read CSV files in parallel; convert the job to a Python shell job.","The S3 bucket is throttling the read; enable S3 Transfer Acceleration."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejalanya: 'single 500 GB gzip-compressed' file dibaca oleh 'a single task' sementara worker lain menganggur. Dalam komputasi terdistribusi, paralelisme baca bergantung pada kemampuan membagi input menjadi split; gzip bukan format yang dapat dibagi (non-splittable), sehingga satu file gzip harus dibaca oleh satu task dari awal sampai akhir. Solusinya adalah banyak file berukuran sedang (misalnya 128 MB–1 GB) atau format/kompresi yang splittable seperti Parquet (dengan Snappy), ORC, atau bzip2. Distractor terdekat adalah menambah worker: worker tambahan tetap menganggur karena hanya ada satu split. Spark dapat membaca CSV tidak terkompresi secara paralel, dan Python shell tidak terdistribusi. Transfer Acceleration untuk upload jarak jauh, bukan untuk paralelisme baca. Aturan umum: satu file gzip besar = satu task; gunakan file terpisah atau format splittable.","r":["Salah — Worker tambahan tetap menganggur karena input hanya satu split.","Benar — Gzip tidak splittable; banyak file atau format splittable memungkinkan pembacaan paralel.","Salah — Spark membaca CSV secara paralel bila file dapat dibagi; Python shell tidak terdistribusi.","Salah — Masalahnya bukan throttling S3; Transfer Acceleration tidak menambah split."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'single task reads one big .gz file' → gzip non-splittable → pecah file / Parquet / bzip2."},{"id":"E3B-65","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"Handling data skew with salting","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job aggregates 3 billion clickstream events with groupBy(merchant_id). One merchant generates about 35% of all events. The stage that performs the aggregation has one task that runs for 2 hours while the other tasks finish in minutes, and adding workers does not help. Which approach will MOST effectively reduce the runtime?","o":["Increase spark.sql.shuffle.partitions to 10,000.","Switch to the G.8X worker type.","Use key salting: add a random salt to merchant_id, aggregate by (merchant_id, salt) first, then aggregate the partial results by merchant_id.","Repartition the input by merchant_id before the aggregation."],"a":[2],"e":"Gejala kuncinya: satu kunci ('one merchant ... 35%') membuat satu task berjalan 2 jam, dan 'adding workers does not help'. Karena semua record dengan kunci yang sama dikirim ke partisi shuffle yang sama, partisi itu menjadi hot spot. Salting menambahkan nilai acak pada kunci sehingga data merchant besar tersebar ke banyak task; agregasi dua tahap (per merchant_id+salt, lalu per merchant_id) menghasilkan hasil akhir yang sama dengan beban yang merata. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah shuffle partitions: kunci yang sama tetap berakhir di satu partisi, sehingga task panas tidak berubah. Worker lebih besar hanya sedikit membantu satu task tersebut. Repartition berdasarkan merchant_id justru memperparah skew. Aturan: skew pada groupBy/join key → salting (atau broadcast join bila satu sisi kecil).","r":["Salah — Menambah partisi tidak memecah satu kunci panas yang tetap masuk ke satu partisi.","Salah — Worker lebih besar tidak memecah beban satu task yang menangani 35% data.","Benar — Salting menyebarkan kunci panas ke banyak task, lalu agregasi kedua menggabungkan hasil parsial.","Salah — Partisi berdasarkan kunci yang skewed justru mengonsentrasikan data ke satu partisi."],"k":"Tips ujian: satu kunci dominan (hot key) di Spark → salting + agregasi dua tahap."},{"id":"E2B-34","d":2,"ts":"2.3.1","t":"Redshift COPY permissions with SSE-KMS","q":"An Amazon Redshift cluster in Account A must run a nightly COPY from an S3 bucket in Account B. The objects are encrypted with SSE-KMS by using a customer managed key in Account B. Security policy forbids long-term access keys in SQL statements. Which TWO actions are required for the COPY command to succeed? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Specify an IAM user's access key ID and secret access key in the COPY command's CREDENTIALS clause.","Associate an IAM role with the cluster that allows s3:GetObject, s3:ListBucket, and kms:Decrypt, and add a bucket policy in Account B that allows that role.","Update the KMS key policy in Account B to allow the Redshift cluster's IAM role to use the key for decryption.","Enable enhanced VPC routing on the Redshift cluster.","Re-encrypt the objects with SSE-S3 in Account B so that no key permissions are needed."],"a":[1,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'bucket in Account B', 'SSE-KMS ... customer managed key in Account B' dan 'forbids long-term access keys'. COPY sebaiknya memakai IAM_ROLE yang terasosiasi ke cluster. Untuk akses lintas akun, role tersebut butuh izin S3 dan kms:Decrypt di policy-nya, dan bucket policy di Account B harus mengizinkan role itu. Karena objek dienkripsi dengan customer managed key milik Account B, key policy di Account B juga harus mengizinkan role dari Account A untuk dekripsi; tanpa itu COPY gagal dengan error akses KMS. Access key di CREDENTIALS melanggar kebijakan keamanan. Enhanced VPC routing mengatur jalur jaringan, bukan izin. Mengganti enkripsi ke SSE-S3 melemahkan kontrol yang ditetapkan pemilik data dan bukan perbaikan yang diminta. Ingat: COPY lintas akun + SSE-KMS → IAM role + bucket policy + key policy.","r":["Salah — Long-term access key di SQL dilarang kebijakan dan bukan praktik terbaik.","Benar — Role di cluster dengan izin S3/KMS, ditambah bucket policy yang mengizinkannya, memberi akses baca lintas akun.","Benar — Customer managed key di akun lain wajib mengizinkan role tersebut lewat key policy agar dekripsi berhasil.","Salah — Enhanced VPC routing mengubah jalur trafik, bukan izin S3 atau KMS.","Salah — Mengubah enkripsi pemilik data menghindari masalah alih-alih mengonfigurasi izin dengan benar."],"k":"Tips ujian: COPY gagal pada data SSE-KMS lintas akun → cek IAM role + bucket policy + KMS key policy."},{"id":"E1A-29","d":1,"ts":"1.1.4","t":"Amazon AppFlow event-triggered flows","q":"A company uses Salesforce as its CRM. The analytics team wants Salesforce account changes to arrive in Amazon S3 within minutes after each change, instead of waiting for a nightly batch. The team wants a managed solution without custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Amazon AppFlow flow that runs on demand and ask users to trigger it after making changes.","Create an Amazon AppFlow flow with Salesforce as the source and Amazon S3 as the destination, and configure the flow to run on event using Salesforce change events.","Use AWS DMS with Salesforce as the source endpoint.","Use AWS Glue crawlers to crawl Salesforce every 5 minutes."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: perubahan Salesforce harus tiba 'within minutes after each change', 'managed', tanpa kode. Amazon AppFlow mendukung tiga jenis trigger: on demand, on schedule, dan on event. Untuk Salesforce, flow bisa dipicu oleh change events (Change Data Capture) sehingga setiap perubahan record dikirim ke S3 hampir real time. Distraktor terdekat adalah flow on demand: bergantung pada tindakan manual pengguna, tidak andal dan tidak otomatis. DMS tidak mendukung Salesforce sebagai sumber. Glue crawler tidak mengambil data dari Salesforce. Aturan umum: AppFlow trigger = on demand / on schedule / on event; perubahan SaaS mendekati real time = on event.","r":["Salah — Bergantung pada pemicu manual sehingga tidak otomatis dan tidak andal.","Benar — AppFlow event-triggered flow dengan Salesforce change events mengirim perubahan dalam hitungan menit tanpa kode.","Salah — AWS DMS tidak mendukung Salesforce sebagai sumber.","Salah — Glue crawler membuat metadata, bukan menyalin data dari Salesforce."],"k":"AppFlow: Salesforce change → near real time → flow trigger 'on event'."},{"id":"E4B-31","d":4,"ts":"4.4.3","t":"Athena partition projection for CloudTrail","q":"A security team queries 2 years of organization CloudTrail logs stored in a central S3 bucket by using Amazon Athena. Most investigations target a single account and a few days, but each query scans the entire bucket, which makes queries slow and expensive. The logs use the standard CloudTrail prefix structure (AWSLogs/account-id/CloudTrail/region/yyyy/mm/dd/). Which change will MOST improve performance and cost?","o":["Configure partition projection on the Athena table for account ID, Region, and date based on the CloudTrail prefix structure, and filter on these partition columns in queries.","Migrate the logs to a new AWS CloudTrail Lake event data store and query them there.","Load the logs into an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster every night with the COPY command.","Increase the Athena workgroup's per-query data scan limit."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya: query 'scans the entire bucket' padahal investigasi hanya menyasar satu akun dan beberapa hari, dan log memakai prefix standar AWSLogs/account-id/CloudTrail/region/yyyy/mm/dd/. Partition projection memungkinkan Athena menghitung partisi dari pola prefix tersebut tanpa harus menjalankan crawler atau MSCK REPAIR, sehingga filter WHERE pada account, Region, dan tanggal hanya membaca prefix yang relevan. Ini menurunkan data yang dipindai (biaya Athena dihitung per TB dipindai) dan mempercepat query. Distraktor terdekat adalah memindahkan ke CloudTrail Lake: selain migrasi dan biaya tambahan, CloudTrail Lake tidak menerima pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026. Load harian ke Redshift menambah biaya cluster dan pipeline. Menaikkan batas scan justru membiarkan query mahal tetap berjalan. Aturan umum: query Athena atas log yang lambat/mahal → partisi (partition projection) + filter partisi, lalu pertimbangkan format kolumnar. Catatan pembaruan: CloudTrail Lake ditutup untuk pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026.","r":["Benar — Partition projection memanfaatkan struktur prefix CloudTrail sehingga query hanya memindai partisi yang relevan.","Salah — Migrasi menambah biaya dan upaya, dan CloudTrail Lake tidak menerima pelanggan baru sejak 31 Mei 2026.","Salah — Redshift menambah biaya cluster dan pipeline load harian untuk kebutuhan investigasi ad hoc.","Salah — Batas scan yang lebih besar tidak mengurangi data yang dipindai; biaya tetap tinggi."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena atas CloudTrail lambat/mahal → partition projection pada account/region/date."},{"id":"E3A-31","d":3,"ts":"3.1.8","t":"Lambda concurrency control with SQS","q":"An AWS Lambda function processes messages from an Amazon SQS queue and writes the results to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. When a large burst of messages arrives, Lambda scales out to hundreds of concurrent invocations, and the database runs out of connections. The data engineer must protect the database while keeping the messages safely in the queue until they can be processed. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Increase the SQS visibility timeout to 12 hours.","Configure the maximum concurrency setting on the SQS event source mapping to a value that the database can handle.","Reduce the SQS message retention period so that old messages are deleted.","Replace the SQS queue with an Amazon SNS topic that invokes the function directly."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'Lambda scales out to hundreds of concurrent invocations', 'database runs out of connections', dan 'keep messages safely in the queue'. Pengaturan maximum concurrency pada SQS event source mapping membatasi berapa banyak invocation bersamaan yang dipicu oleh queue tersebut. Pesan berlebih tetap aman di SQS dan diproses saat kapasitas tersedia, sehingga database terlindungi. Reserved concurrency juga bisa membatasi, tetapi dapat menyebabkan throttling dan pesan kembali ke queue; maximum concurrency adalah kontrol yang lebih tepat untuk sumber SQS. Visibility timeout 12 jam hanya menunda retry dan tidak membatasi concurrency. Mengurangi retensi justru menghapus data. SNS memicu Lambda secara push tanpa buffer, sehingga lonjakan malah langsung menghantam database. Aturan umum: lindungi downstream dari lonjakan Lambda → batasi concurrency, biarkan SQS menjadi buffer.","r":["Salah — Visibility timeout panjang tidak membatasi jumlah invocation bersamaan dan memperlambat retry.","Benar — Maximum concurrency pada event source mapping membatasi invocation, dan sisa pesan menunggu di SQS.","Salah — Mengurangi retensi berisiko menghapus pesan yang belum diproses.","Salah — SNS tidak menyediakan buffer, sehingga lonjakan langsung membebani database."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Lambda membanjiri database dari SQS' → maximum concurrency pada SQS event source mapping (SQS sebagai buffer)."}]});